{"Q": {"id": "Q01", "question": "How is the Conflict deck built, and what happens to unused Conflict cards?"}, "K": {"id": "Q01", "expected_answer": "Shuffle all four III cards at the bottom, five randomly dealt of nine II cards above, one randomly dealt of three I cards on top: ten total. Return unused cards to the box without looking.", "source_references": "Main PDF p4 / extraction 190–209", "novelty": "Conflict deck construction"}, "R": {"id": "Q01", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [178, 191]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q01", "answer": "Shuffle all four Conflict III cards and put them face down at the bottom; shuffle all nine II cards and deal five face down above them; shuffle all three I cards and deal one face down on top. Return unused I and II cards to the box unseen.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup: shuffle/deal results in a face-down 10-card Conflict Deck; return unused Conflict cards without looking."}, "B": {"id": "Q01", "answer": "Shuffle the four Conflict III cards and place all four face down at the bottom; shuffle the nine II cards and deal five face down above them; shuffle the three I cards and deal one face down on top. Return unused cards to the box unseen; the shuffle-and-deal selects which I and II cards are used.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup, lines 53, 60-68: face-down 10-card deck, I on top, five II, four III; return unused cards unseen."}}
