d pile.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Turn Structure, lines 91, 97-100: Reveal is allowed with Agents left; revealed cards only resolve Reveal boxes; all cards in front move to discard."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q04", "question": "May an Agent-turn card effect provide resources to pay the destination entry cost? How many Agents can one card send, and can a card without Agent icons be used?"}, "K": {"id": "Q04", "expected_answer": "Entry costs paid immediately before any card or space effects; cannot use later gains to pay entry. One card sends one Agent using one matching icon. No-icon card cannot be played on an Agent turn.", "source_references": "Main p9 / extraction 425–452", "novelty": "Entry legality and costs"}, "R": {"id": "Q04", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [424, 448]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q04", "answer": "No: destination entry costs must be paid immediately before resolving any board-space or played-card effects, so an Agent-box effect cannot pay that entry. One card sends only one Agent, using one Agent icon. A card with no Agent icons cannot be played on an Agent turn and may only be revealed.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Agent Turn: pay costs immediately before resolving effects; choose only one Agent icon; card with no Agent icons may only be revealed."}, "B": {"id": "Q04", "answer": "A resource granted by a Plot Intrigue played before Agent placement can pay the entry cost. A resource gained only after placement from the Agent card or destination cannot pay that same cost. One card sends one Agent using only one icon. A card with no Agent icons cannot be used on an Agent turn; it may only be revealed.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Turn Structure, lines 91, 95: pre-placement Plot gains can pay; post-placement gains cannot; one Agent icon and no-icon restriction."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q05", "question": "At a Combat space you recruit three troops this turn and already have four garrisoned. How many can deploy? What if the destination is not a Combat space, and where do recruited troops originate?"}, "K": {"id": "Q05", "expected_answer": "May deploy all three newly recruited plus at most two older garrison troops, five total. Normal deployment unavailable at noncombat space. Recruit from own supply into garrison; empty supply prevents recruiting.", "source_references": "Main p10 / extraction 535–566", "novelty": "Recruit and deployment limits"}, "R": {"id": "Q05", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [532, 555]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q05", "answer": "At a Combat space, all three troops recruited this turn may deploy, plus up to two additional troops from the four already in your garrison: at most five total. At a non-Combat space, troops cannot deploy and remain in the garrison. Recruited troops are taken from your supply and placed in the garrison first.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Recruiting & Deploying: troop recruitment takes a troop from supply into garrison; at a Combat space deploy any/all recruited this turn plus up to two more from garrison."}, "B": {"id": "Q05", "answer": "At a Combat space, you can deploy the three troops recruited that turn plus up to two more from your garrison: five total in this example. At a non-Combat space you cannot deploy units. Troops are recruited from your supply into your garrison; recruited troops eligible to deploy include those from the board space and played card this turn.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Recruiting & Deploying, line 128: current-turn recruits plus up to two garrison units at Combat spaces; troop recruitment takes from supply to garrison."}}

