{"Q": {"id": "Q06", "question": "How do you use a Spy Agent icon, Infiltrate and Gather Intelligence? Can the same Spy pay for both, and when must Gather Intelligence be chosen?"}, "K": {"id": "Q06", "expected_answer": "Spy Agent icon permits a connected space without recalling Spy. Infiltrate recalls own connected Spy to bypass another player Agent. Gather Intelligence recalls own connected Spy to draw, chosen immediately after placement before card/space effects. Same Spy cannot do both; separate Spies can.", "source_references": "Main p11 / extraction 606–622", "novelty": "Distinct spy functions and timing"}, "R": {"id": "Q06", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [590, 609]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q06", "answer": "A Spy Agent icon lets you send an Agent to a space connected to an observation post where you have a Spy; it does not recall that Spy. Infiltrate recalls your Spy at a connected post to bypass another player's Agent at the destination, not your own. Gather Intelligence recalls a connected Spy to draw a card; choose immediately after placing your Agent, before receiving space or card effects. The same Spy cannot pay for both Infiltrate and Gather Intelligence, though separate Spies can. You must still play an appropriate card for the Agent turn.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Special Rules—Spies: Spy Agent icon does not recall; Infiltrate bypasses another player's occupancy; Gather Intelligence choice is immediately after placement; cannot recall same Spy for both."}, "B": {"id": "Q06", "answer": "A Spy Agent icon lets you send an Agent to a space connected to a post where you have a Spy, without recalling that Spy; a normal icon on the card can also authorize access where matching. Infiltrate recalls your Spy from a connected post to enter another player's occupied space, ignoring that occupancy; it cannot bypass your own Agent. Gather Intelligence recalls a connected Spy to draw a card, chosen immediately after Agent placement and before the space or card effects. The same Spy cannot pay both Infiltrate and Gather Intelligence.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Special Rules, line 160: Spy Agent access does not recall; Infiltrate and Gather Intelligence descriptions and timing; cannot recall same Spy for both."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q07", "question": "With two troops, one sandworm and four revealed swords, what is your strength? What if your final unit is removed? Can you participate in Combat Intrigue with no unit?"}, "K": {"id": "Q07", "expected_answer": "Strength 11 (2+2+3+4). No units means zero strength regardless swords. Without a unit cannot participate in Combat Intrigue.", "source_references": "Main pp12,14 / extraction 652–665,744–750", "novelty": "Strength and eligibility"}, "R": {"id": "Q07", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [658, 667]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [743, 748]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q07", "answer": "Strength is 11 (two troops at 2 each, one sandworm at 3, and four revealed swords at 1 each). If your last unit is removed, strength becomes 0. With no unit in the Conflict, you may not participate in Combat Intrigue.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Strength: each troop 2, each sandworm 3, each revealed sword 1; if last unit removed strength is 0. Combat Intrigue requires at least one unit in Conflict."}, "B": {"id": "Q07", "answer": "Strength is 2 troops × 2, plus one sandworm × 3, plus four swords × 1, totaling 11. If the final unit is removed, strength becomes 0. A player with no unit in the Conflict cannot participate in the Combat Intrigue window.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Strength, lines 121-122: troops 2, sandworm 3, sword 1; no units means 0; Combat, line 103 requires at least one unit for Combat Intrigue."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q08", "question": "If you pass Combat Intrigue and an opponent then plays one, may you act again? When does the window close, and where do troops and sandworms go after rewards?"}, "K": {"id": "Q08", "expected_answer": "May act again after earlier pass; closes only when all involved players pass consecutively. Adjust strength for effects. After all rewards troops return to supply not garrison, sandworms to bank, Combat markers reset zero.", "source_references": "Main p14 / extraction 744–750,767–769", "novelty": "Combat priority and cleanup"}, "R": {"id": "Q08", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [743, 748]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [768, 769]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q08", "answer": "Yes, you may act again after passing if an opponent plays a Combat Intrigue; the window closes when all players involved pass consecutively. After rewards, troops return to their supply (not garrison) and sandworms to the bank.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Combat: you are not required to pass because you passed earlier; resolve after consecutive passes. Cleanup returns troops to supply and sandworms to bank."}, "B": {"id": "Q08", "answer": "Yes. Passing once does not prevent acting again if another player acts; the window closes after all players involved in Combat pass consecutively. After rewards, troops return to their supply (not garrison), and sandworms return to the bank.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Combat, lines 103, 110: may act after earlier pass; consecutive passes close; troops to supply, sandworms to bank."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q09", "question": "Compare two players tied for first in a four-player Conflict with the same tie in a three-player Conflict. Who takes the Conflict card, and can a zero-strength player get a reward?"}, "K": {"id": "Q09", "expected_answer": "Each tied first gets second reward and nobody wins or takes card. In four-player game remaining players compete for third; in three-player game no further rewards. Zero strength never rewarded.", "source_references": "Main p14 / extraction 765,792–808", "novelty": "Tie for first outcome branches"}, "R": {"id": "Q09", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [751, 806]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q09", "answer": "If two players tie for first in four-player play, each gets the second reward; the remaining players compete for the third reward, but nobody wins or takes the Conflict card. In a three-player game, tied first players each get second reward, no other reward is given, and nobody takes the card. A zero-strength player gets no reward.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Combat ties: exactly two tied first with four players means remaining players compete for third; nobody takes the card. Three or fewer tied first: second reward only. Zero strength receives no reward."}, "B": {"id": "Q09", "answer": "With two tied for first in a four-player game, each gets the second reward and the remaining players compete for the third reward; nobody wins or takes the Conflict card. With the same tie in a three-player game, each tied player gets second reward and there are no other rewards; nobody takes the card. A zero-strength player receives no reward.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Combat, lines 105-110 and tie table lines 175-181; zero strength receives no reward."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q10", "question": "What does a sandworm do to rewards: do two sandworms quadruple them, can control or battle icons double, and how is a reward offering 3 spice for 1 VP handled?"}, "K": {"id": "Q10", "expected_answer": "One or more sandworms doubles, never quadruples. Control and battle icons do not double. Optional reward cost may be paid second time: 3 spice for 1 VP or 6 for 2, not free second VP.", "source_references": "Main p14 / extraction 778–791", "novelty": "Doubling scope and cost exception"}, "R": {"id": "Q10", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [779, 787]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q10", "answer": "One or more sandworms double rewards once; two sandworms do not quadruple them. Control of a location and battle icons on won Conflict cards are not doubled. A reward offering 3 spice for 1 VP may be paid a second time under doubling: pay another 3 spice for another 1 VP, or 6 total spice for 2 VP.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Sandworm Reward Doubling: one or more sandworms double; control and battle icons cannot; optional reward cost may be paid a second time, with example 3 spice for 1 VP or 6 for 2."}, "B": {"id": "Q10", "answer": "One or more sandworms double the rewards you take; two worms do not quadruple them. Taking control of a location and battle icons on won Conflict cards cannot be doubled. For a reward allowing 3 spice for 1 VP, you may pay the cost a second time under doubling: pay 3 spice for the first VP, or 6 spice for 2 VP.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Sandworm Reward Doubling, line 137: one or more double; control and battle icons excluded; optional reward cost may be paid twice."}}

