{"Q": {"id": "Q11", "question": "When is a normal battle-icon match checked, which cards qualify, is matching optional, and how is a wild icon used?"}, "K": {"id": "Q11", "expected_answer": "After winning and taking Conflict card face up in supply check another face-up Conflict or Objective with same icon; must flip pair face down for 1 VP. At Endgame wild can match any of three icons in supply, pair flipped for 1 VP.", "source_references": "Main p14,p20 / extraction 770–777,1090–1096", "novelty": "Battle icon match"}, "R": {"id": "Q11", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [770, 778]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1114, 1120]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q11", "answer": "After winning and taking the Conflict card face up into your supply, check for another face-up Conflict or Objective card with a matching battle icon. If present, matching is mandatory: flip the pair face down for 1 VP. In Endgame, the wild icon may match any one of the three icons in your supply, flipping the pair for 1 VP.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Battle Icons: when you win and take card, check face-up Conflict or Objective cards; must flip matching pair; during Endgame wild may match any icon."}, "B": {"id": "Q11", "answer": "When you win and take the Conflict card, first put it face up in your supply, then check for a match. Face-up Conflict or Objective cards with the same icon qualify. The matching pair must be flipped face down and scores 1 VP, so it is mandatory. During Endgame, a wild icon may match any one of the three icons in your supply; flip the pair for 1 VP.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Combat, lines 107-108; Battle Icons, line 140: winner's check after card acquisition, matching face-up cards, must flip, wild at Endgame."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q12", "question": "What are the rewards and reversibility at 2 and 4 Faction Influence, and does tying the Alliance holder at 4 steal the Alliance?"}, "K": {"id": "Q12", "expected_answer": "Reach 2 gets 1 VP lost below 2. Reach 4 gets track bonus retained if falling below, can earn again on re-reaching. First to 4 gets Alliance and its VP; tie does not steal, opponent must rise higher. Transfer loses old holder VP and gives new holder VP.", "source_references": "Main p7 / extraction 333–344", "novelty": "Influence thresholds and Alliance"}, "R": {"id": "Q12", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [325, 337]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q12", "answer": "At 2 Influence, gain 1 VP, lose it below 2, and regain it on reaching 2 again. At 4, gain the printed track bonus, which is retained after falling below 4 and earned again on returning to 4; the first to 4 also gets the Alliance token and its 1 VP, which remains only while held. Tying the Alliance holder does not take it; gaining more Influence transfers it. If the holder loses Influence after having been tied, the FAQ says the formerly tied opponent takes it (or the former holder chooses among multiple tied opponents).", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Faction Influence: 2 Influence VP reverses below 2; 4 Influence has separate retained track bonus and Alliance VP; tying does not steal; FAQ gives transfer on holder losing Influence after tie."}, "B": {"id": "Q12", "answer": "At 2 Influence, gain 1 VP; falling below 2 loses it, and reaching 2 again regains it. At 4, gain the printed track bonus, which is retained after falling below 4 and earned again on returning to 4; the first player to 4 also gains the Alliance and its 1 VP, which follows its holder. Tying the Alliance holder does not steal it: a challenger must rise above the holder. The separate FAQ trigger is a holder losing Influence after being tied; then the formerly tied opponent takes it, or if several were tied the former holder chooses the recipient.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Scoring, line 153: 2 VP, 4 track bonus reversal, Alliance tied to holder, rise above to transfer; FAQ transfer trigger."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q13", "question": "When can Persuasion be spent during Reveal, may it be pooled or split, can you buy a Row replacement immediately, and where does the acquired card go?"}, "K": {"id": "Q13", "expected_answer": "Before between or after Reveal effects; can pool and split. Refill Row to five immediately; may buy replacement with remaining Persuasion. Acquired card face-up discard, cannot use immediately; unspent Persuasion lost.", "source_references": "Main pp12–13 / extraction 645–649,704–730", "novelty": "Acquisition timing and destination"}, "R": {"id": "Q13", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [652, 656]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [704, 733]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q13", "answer": "Persuasion can be spent during Reveal before, between, or after Reveal effects. It may be pooled from multiple sources for one card or split across cards. The Imperium Row refills immediately to five, so you may acquire a replacement in the same Reveal if you can afford it. Acquired cards go face up into your discard pile.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Acquiring Cards: may use Persuasion before/between/after effects, pool or split; Row always has five and replacement may be acquired; acquired card goes face up to discard."}, "B": {"id": "Q13", "answer": "Persuasion is spent during the Reveal turn, before, between, or after Reveal effects. It may be pooled from multiple sources to buy one card and split from one source across cards. The Imperium Row is refilled to five, and you may buy a replacement immediately if able. An acquired card goes face up into your discard pile.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Acquiring Cards, line 143: timing, pool/split, row refill/replacement purchase, discard destination."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q14", "question": "How do Maker bonus spice, the Shield Wall and Maker Hooks affect harvesting and summoning, and where can a sandworm be placed?"}, "K": {"id": "Q14", "expected_answer": "Makers phase adds one bonus spice on each unoccupied Maker space, accumulating; visiting collects all bonus spice. Shield Wall blocks worms at Arrakeen, Spice Refinery, Imperial Basin until removed to box. Maker Hooks prerequisite when specified; summoning directly bank to Conflict, never garrison.", "source_references": "Main pp10,15,20 / extraction 493–522,567–584,835–845,1130–1135", "novelty": "Maker and worm restrictions"}, "R": {"id": "Q14", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [509, 568]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [832, 838]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1150, 1156]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q14", "answer": "At Makers phase, add 1 spice to each Agent-free Maker space; when visiting a Maker space, take all accumulated bonus spice there. Summoning a sandworm places it directly in the Conflict, never in a garrison, and usually requires Maker Hooks if the effect specifies that prerequisite; Hooks are retained, not spent. While the Shield Wall remains, a worm cannot be summoned to Arrakeen, Spice Refinery, or Imperial Basin; removing the Wall permits summons to any Conflict. The summary says Hooks and Wall requirements depend on the particular summoning effect.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Makers: add spice if space unoccupied; visit gains all. Sandworms: summon immediately to Conflict; specified Hooks prerequisite; Shield Wall protects three named locations; removal permits any Conflict."}, "B": {"id": "Q14", "answer": "At Makers, each empty Maker space gets one spice added to any accumulated bonus; visiting a Maker space collects all bonus spice there, including when choosing worms. Hagga Basin and Deep Desert offer base spice or, with Maker Hooks, one and two sandworms respectively. Hooks are required only when the summoning effect specifies them and are retained, not spent. A sandworm cannot go in a garrison; while Shield Wall remains it cannot be summoned to Arrakeen, Spice Refinery, or Imperial Basin. Once the Wall is removed, any Conflict is eligible.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Makers line 113; Sandworms lines 131-134; Deep Desert/Hagga table lines 227,234."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q15", "question": "At what point does 10 VP or an empty Conflict deck end play, what happens before comparing final VP, and what are the rulebook resource tiebreakers?"}, "K": {"id": "Q15", "expected_answer": "Check in Recall at end of round, not immediately at 10 VP. Resolve Endgame Intrigue first then highest VP wins. Ties spice then Solari then water then garrisoned troops.", "source_references": "Main pp15 / extraction 824–855", "novelty": "End trigger and scoring"}, "R": {"id": "Q15", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [824, 848]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q15", "answer": "At Recall, if anyone has 10+ VP or the Conflict Deck is empty, Endgame is triggered. Before comparing VP, players may play and resolve Endgame Intrigue cards. Most VP wins; ties break in order by spice, Solari, water, then garrisoned troops.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Scoring: at end of round threshold or empty deck triggers Endgame; first resolve Endgame Intrigue, then highest VP wins; listed tiebreakers."}, "B": {"id": "Q15", "answer": "At Recall at the end of a round, 10 or more VP for any player or an empty Conflict Deck triggers Endgame. Players first may play and resolve any Endgame Intrigue cards, then compare VP; the most VP wins. The rulebook resource tiebreakers in order are spice, Solari, water, then garrisoned troops.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Scoring, line 150 and Recall line 116: Endgame trigger, Endgame Intrigue then most VP; listed tiebreakers."}}

