{"Q": {"id": "Q16", "question": "With optional standard CHOAM, how many contracts start face up and face down, which extra cards are added, is Shaddam compulsory, and are the 10 contrasting-back contracts part of this standard setup?"}, "K": {"id": "Q16", "expected_answer": "20 standard contracts: two face up, eighteen in bank. Add four Intrigue and four Imperium; Shaddam optional. Ten contrasting-back contracts are only Rise of Ix compatibility, excluded from standard setup.", "source_references": "Main p16 / extraction 860–879,916–936", "novelty": "CHOAM setup and compatibility boundary"}, "R": {"id": "Q16", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [850, 932]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q16", "answer": "Standard CHOAM setup has two contracts face up and the rest of the standard 20 face down in the bank: 18 in bank without Shaddam, or 16 plus two set-aside Sardaukar contracts if Shaddam is chosen. Add four CHOAM Imperium cards and four CHOAM Intrigue cards. Shaddam is optional and usable only with CHOAM. The 10 contrasting-back Rise of Ix contracts stay in the box.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "CHOAM setup changes: two face up; 20 standard, set aside two for Shaddam when chosen; add four additional Intrigue and four Imperium cards; contrasting-back set is Rise of Ix only."}, "B": {"id": "Q16", "answer": "Standard CHOAM starts with two contracts face up as offers and the remaining 18 face down in the bank. Add four CHOAM Imperium cards and four CHOAM Intrigue cards to their respective decks. Shaddam is optional. The ten contrasting-back contracts are for Rise of Ix compatibility and stay in the box; they are not part of this setup.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "CHOAM setup, lines 194, 206: two offers and 18 bank without Shaddam; four extra cards of each type; Shaddam optional; contrasting contracts excluded."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q17", "question": "Under CHOAM, what does the contract icon do, what if all contracts are taken, and how are Harvest, Immediate and Acquire The Spice Must Flow contracts completed?"}, "K": {"id": "Q17", "expected_answer": "Take one of two face-up into supply then refill face up from bank; if all taken gain 2 Solari (also without module). Harvest: visit Maker and gain specified total spice that turn including other sources. Immediate upon taking. Acquire The Spice Must Flow on next acquiring that card.", "source_references": "Main p16 / extraction 880–901", "novelty": "CHOAM taking and types"}, "R": {"id": "Q17", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [868, 885]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q17", "answer": "With CHOAM, the contract icon lets you take one of two face-up contracts and replace it from the bank; if players have taken all contracts, the icon instead gives 2 Solari. A Harvest contract completes when you send an Agent to a Maker space and gain its stated spice amount that turn, including spice from other sources. Immediate completes as soon as taken. Acquire The Spice Must Flow completes when you next acquire that card.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Taking contracts and Completing contracts: icon takes face-up contract and replaces; exhausted supply gives 2 Solari; definitions of Harvest, Immediate, and Acquire contracts."}, "B": {"id": "Q17", "answer": "With CHOAM, the contract icon lets you take one of two face-up contracts and replace it with a face-up contract from the bank; if all contracts have been taken by players, it gives 2 Solari instead. A Harvest contract completes by visiting a Maker space and gaining the shown amount of spice during that turn in total, including other sources. Immediate completes upon taking it. Acquire The Spice Must Flow completes when you next acquire that card.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Taking contracts line 196; Completing contracts lines 199-202."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q18", "question": "You gain a board-space contract after already sending your Agent to that space this turn. Can you complete it now? Once completed what do you announce, gain and do with the token?"}, "K": {"id": "Q18", "expected_answer": "Cannot complete now; must have held contract when Agent sent, wait future turn. Announce completion, gain printed rewards, flip face down and leave in supply.", "source_references": "Main p16 / extraction 902–907", "novelty": "CHOAM ownership timing and destination"}, "R": {"id": "Q18", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [886, 890]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q18", "answer": "No. If you take a contract for a space after already sending your Agent there this turn, you must wait until a future turn; you must hold the contract when sending the Agent. When completing a contract, announce it, gain its shown rewards, then flip it face down and leave it in your supply.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Completing contracts: already-visited space contract waits until future turn; must have contract at placement; announce, gain rewards, flip face down and leave in supply."}, "B": {"id": "Q18", "answer": "No. If you take a contract for a space after already sending your Agent there this turn, you must wait until a future turn; you must hold the contract at the time you send the Agent. When completing it, announce it, gain its shown rewards, then flip it face down and leave it in your supply.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Completing contracts, line 204: must have contract at placement; announce, gain rewards, flip down and retain in supply."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q19", "question": "In standard two-player play how many Rivals are used, who gets the Ornithopter Objective, who gets First Player, what is the turn order, and does a Rival Reveal?"}, "K": {"id": "Q19", "expected_answer": "One shared Rival. Rival gets Ornithopter Objective, other two randomly humans; Rival never First Player. Marker alternates humans, Rival considered clockwise from First Player and acts between humans each round. Takes Agent turns while it has Agent in supply, never Reveals.", "source_references": "Supplements PDF pp3–4", "novelty": "Required two-player setup and turn order"}, "R": {"id": "Q19", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [191, 204]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [226, 232]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q19", "answer": "Use one shared scoring Rival as the third competitor. It receives the Ornithopter Objective; the other two eligible Objectives are dealt randomly to humans, and the human with the First Player marker on their Objective goes first. Turn order is First Player, Rival, other human; the Rival takes Agent turns while it has Agents and never Reveals.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Required Rival Rules: one shared scoring Rival; Rival gets Ornithopter Objective; First Player determined from human card; order First Player → Rival → other human; Rival never Reveal."}, "B": {"id": "Q19", "answer": "Standard two-player play uses one shared scoring Rival. The Rival gets the Ornithopter Objective; the other two eligible Objectives are dealt to the humans. First Player goes to the human whose card shows it, and alternates only between humans. Each round order is First Player → Rival → other human. The Rival never Reveals.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival setup and Agent turns, lines 251-253: one shared Rival; objective/first player/turn order; never takes Reveal."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q20", "question": "A Rival reveals an occupied board space, then a Place Spy card. How does it proceed, which space costs and effects apply, and what happens when House Hagal is empty or Reshuffle is drawn?"}, "K": {"id": "Q20", "expected_answer": "Occupied: ignore and reveal again. Place Spy tries empty designated post, ignore placement if none, then reveal another card regardless because no Agent sent. Ignore normal space costs/effects; use Hagal effects only. Empty deck or Reshuffle: immediately reshuffle Hagal and continue.", "source_references": "Supplements PDF p4", "novelty": "Rival card resolution"}, "R": {"id": "Q20", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [233, 269]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q20", "answer": "A Rival ignores an occupied destination and reveals another House Hagal card until it can place on an unoccupied indicated space. A Place Spy card does not place an Agent: use a free post of the specified type if one exists, otherwise ignore that placement; then reveal another Hagal card and continue the Agent turn. Rival ignores normal space costs and effects and applies only Hagal effects. If Hagal empties or Reshuffle appears, immediately reshuffle and continue. The summary does not enumerate the costs and effects of every board space, but establishes they are ignored for the Rival.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Agent turns: occupied destinations ignored and reveal again; Place Spy no Agent and reveal another; ignores normal space costs/effects; reshuffle immediately."}, "B": {"id": "Q20", "answer": "For an occupied destination, the Rival ignores it and reveals another Hagal card. A Place Spy card does not place an Agent: try an empty post of the specified type, ignore the placement if none exists, then reveal another Hagal card and continue the same Agent turn. Ignore ordinary board-space costs and effects; apply only revealed Hagal effects. If Hagal empties or Reshuffle appears, immediately reshuffle and continue.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival rules, lines 253-257: occupied destination, Place Spy continuation, ignore normal space effects/costs, reshuffle behavior."}}

