{"Q": {"id": "Q21", "question": "How are eligible Objective cards selected and distributed in standard three- or four-player setup, how is First Player chosen, and may Shaddam be chosen without CHOAM?"}, "K": {"id": "Q21", "expected_answer": "Omit Objectives whose 1–3P or 4/6P mark mismatches count; shuffle, each takes one random face up in supply. First Player is holder of marked Objective. Shaddam cannot be chosen without CHOAM.", "source_references": "Main pp4–5 / extraction 210–220,254–263", "novelty": "Objective eligibility and Leader restriction"}, "R": {"id": "Q21", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [193, 195]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [237, 242]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q21", "answer": "Omit Objective cards whose player-count marking does not match, shuffle eligible cards, and distribute one face up to each player. The Objective marked with the First Player marker determines the human First Player; in standard three- and four-player setup the summary gives no more specific Objective selection procedure beyond matching the count and random distribution. Shaddam cannot be chosen without CHOAM.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup: omit mismatched Objective cards, shuffle and deal face up; marked Objective determines First Player. Shaddam is not used unless playing with CHOAM."}, "B": {"id": "Q21", "answer": "For three or four players, omit Objective cards whose printed player-count marking does not match, shuffle the eligible cards, and distribute one face up to each player; the card marked First Player determines who starts. Shaddam may be used only with the CHOAM Module, so he may not be chosen without CHOAM.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup, lines 54, 56: choose Leader but Shaddam only with CHOAM; filter, shuffle and distribute eligible objectives face up, marked First Player."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q22", "question": "If the bank runs out of Solari, spice, water or sandworms, what happens? Contrast an empty personal troop supply, and state where resource payments go."}, "K": {"id": "Q22", "expected_answer": "Bank resources and sandworms not limited; substitute conveniently. Cannot recruit troops from empty personal supply until returned. Resource gains come from bank and payments return to bank.", "source_references": "Main pp5,10,20 / extraction 273–279,535–539,1152–1154", "novelty": "Component exhaustion and bank destinations"}, "R": {"id": "Q22", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [255, 260]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [532, 536]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1171, 1173]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q22", "answer": "The bank's Solari, spice, water and sandworms are not limited; use any convenient substitution if they run out. Troops are different: if your personal supply has no troops, you cannot recruit more until troops return to it. Resource gains come from the bank and payments return to the bank.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup bank: resources and sandworms not meant to be limited; substitute as needed. Recruit from supply; if empty cannot recruit; gain from bank and payments return to bank."}, "B": {"id": "Q22", "answer": "The bank resources and sandworms are not limited; if the bank runs out, make a convenient substitution. By contrast, if your personal troop supply is empty, you cannot recruit more until some troops return to it. Resource payments for Solari, spice, and water go back to the bank; gains come from the bank, not another player's supply.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup, lines 57-58: empty troop supply rule, bank not limited, take gains from bank and return payments."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q23", "question": "State all five round phases in order, when Conflict and hand cards are drawn, and what Recall does if Endgame is not triggered."}, "K": {"id": "Q23", "expected_answer": "Round Start, Player Turns, Combat, Makers, Recall. Start reveals top Conflict face up atop previous remaining cards then each draws five. If no Endgame, recall Agents to Leaders, pass First Player clockwise and begin next round (two-player Rival exception).", "source_references": "Main pp8,15 / extraction 355–360,385–390,824–834", "novelty": "Round order and restart"}, "R": {"id": "Q23", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [354, 382]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [824, 840]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q23", "answer": "The five phases are Round Start, Player Turns, Combat, Makers, Recall. At Round Start reveal a Conflict card and each player draws five cards. If Endgame is not triggered at Recall, players recall Agents to Leaders, pass First Player clockwise, and start the next round.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Turn Structure and Player Reference: ordered phases; Round Start reveals Conflict and draws five; Recall prepares next round by recalling Agents and passing First Player."}, "B": {"id": "Q23", "answer": "The five phases are Round Start, Player Turns, Combat, Makers, Recall. At Round Start reveal a Conflict card, resolve the controlled-location defensive troop bonus if applicable, then each player draws five cards. If Endgame is not triggered at Recall, players return Agents to their Leaders, pass First Player clockwise, and begin the next round.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Turn Structure, lines 85-88, 112-116: phase order, Conflict reveal then five-card draw, Recall procedure."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q24", "question": "May you resolve board-space effects, Agent-box effects and Faction Influence in any order? Can you use that visit’s Influence to meet its entry requirement?"}, "K": {"id": "Q24", "expected_answer": "Resolve effects in any order after placement, but entry requirements and costs must be met before any effects. Cannot rely on Influence gained by the visit for its entry requirement.", "source_references": "Main p9 / extraction 403–409,439–452,482–489", "novelty": "Effect-order versus entry requirement priority"}, "R": {"id": "Q24", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [403, 448]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [482, 489]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q24", "answer": "Yes. Space effects, played card Agent-box effects, and the Faction Influence advance may be resolved in any order. No: the entry cost and requirements must be met immediately before resolving any space or card effects, so Influence gained from the visit cannot satisfy that visit's requirement.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Agent Turn: pay costs and meet requirements immediately before effects; gain space and Agent-box effects and Faction Influence; may carry out all effects in any order."}, "B": {"id": "Q24", "answer": "Yes. Board-space effects, Agent-box effects, and the Faction Influence advance may be carried out in any order. But entry requirements and costs must be met before placement and before any space or played-card effects resolve, so Influence from that visit cannot meet its entry requirement.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Agent Turn, line 95: pay costs/meet requirements first, then effects and Influence in any order."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q25", "question": "Can an optional arrow cost be paid twice in an Agent turn? Which effects are normally optional or mandatory, including costs on Intrigue cards?"}, "K": {"id": "Q25", "expected_answer": "Only once per turn, except sandworm-doubled Conflict rewards. Most effects mandatory except may, optional arrow payment and black-X trash. Direct self-trash mandatory. All Intrigue conditions/costs required to play it.", "source_references": "Main pp9,20; FAQ p3 optional effects/paying a cost", "novelty": "Optional effect boundary and Intrigue exception"}, "R": {"id": "Q25", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [414, 420]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1157, 1162]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [175, 180]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [213, 229]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q25", "answer": "No. An optional arrow cost and effect can be paid and gained only once per turn, except sandworm doubling of a Conflict reward. Most card and space effects are mandatory; exceptions include 'may,' optional arrow costs, and optional black-X trash. Intrigue costs and conditions must be met to play it; all costs must be paid. Trashing is optional unless it pays a cost or a card directs you to trash itself.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Arrows: may pay/gain only once per turn except doubled Conflict rewards. FAQ: most effects mandatory with stated exceptions; Intrigue costs/conditions must be met. Trashing section explains exceptions."}, "B": {"id": "Q25", "answer": "An optional arrow cost/effect may be paid and resolved only once per turn, not twice. Most card and space effects are mandatory; exceptions include effects stated as “may,” arrow costs that can be declined, and the optional black-X trash icon. Intrigue conditions and costs must be met to play the Intrigue.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Arrows line 165; FAQ line 281: once-per-turn arrow exception; mandatory effects and optional exceptions; Intrigue conditions/costs."}}

