{"Q": {"id": "Q26", "question": "Where may a new Spy be placed, what if all your Spies are already deployed, and what if its placement effect specifies an Agent-icon type?"}, "K": {"id": "Q26", "expected_answer": "Unoccupied observation post, from supply. If none in supply may first recall one of own Spies for no effect. Specified icon must connect to post or cannot place there.", "source_references": "Main p11 / extraction 588–605", "novelty": "Spy placement and exhaustion"}, "R": {"id": "Q26", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [576, 589]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q26", "answer": "A Spy may be placed from supply on an unoccupied observation post. If you have no Spies in supply, you may first recall one for no effect. If the placement effect specifies an Agent-icon type that must connect to the post, you may only place at a post connected to that icon; otherwise you cannot place the Spy.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Spies & observation posts: place on unoccupied post; may recall one if none in supply; some effects require a particular Agent icon connected to post."}, "B": {"id": "Q26", "answer": "Place a Spy from your supply on an unoccupied observation post connected to spaces, subject to any specified Agent-icon type. If you have no Spy in supply, you may first recall one of your Spies for no effect to free it. If the placement effect specifies an Agent icon that must be connected to the post, the post must meet that condition; otherwise you cannot place there.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Special Rules, line 160: unoccupied post; recall Spy if supply empty; specific connected Agent icon requirement."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q27", "question": "Can you Infiltrate your own occupied board space, use a Spy without playing a card, or recall two connected Spies to Gather Intelligence twice on one placement?"}, "K": {"id": "Q27", "expected_answer": "No to all. Infiltrate bypasses another player Agent; still play a card and meet entry costs/requirements. Two Spies can pay different effects (Infiltrate and Gather Intelligence), not duplicate Gather Intelligence.", "source_references": "Main p11; FAQ p4 Spies", "novelty": "Spy ownership and per-effect recall limits"}, "R": {"id": "Q27", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [590, 609]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [327, 333]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q27", "answer": "No, Infiltrate cannot bypass your own Agent. A Spy may be recalled without playing a card for Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence, but the recall still requires playing a card for the Agent turn and does not waive costs or requirements. No, you cannot recall two Spies to Gather Intelligence twice on one placement; two Spies may be recalled for different effects, one to Infiltrate and one to Gather Intelligence.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Infiltrate only bypasses another player; FAQ says recall requires card for Agent turn; cannot use two to Gather Intelligence, but may use one for each different effect."}, "B": {"id": "Q27", "answer": "No, Infiltrate only bypasses another player's Agent, not your own. A Spy cannot be used without playing a card for an Agent turn to recall it. You cannot recall two connected Spies to Gather Intelligence twice on the same placement; you may use separate Spies for Infiltrate and Gather Intelligence.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Special Rules line 160 and FAQ line 285: own occupancy exclusion; card still required; one Gather Intelligence, but distinct Spy for each different effect."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q28", "question": "Who gets control bonuses when visiting Arrakeen, Spice Refinery or Imperial Basin, how is control transferred, and where does the defensive troop originate?"}, "K": {"id": "Q28", "expected_answer": "Winning respective Conflict puts control marker on flag replacing opponent. Controller receives 1 Solari at Arrakeen/Refinery or 1 spice at Basin whenever anyone including self visits. Reveal of controlled location Conflict permits one troop from supply directly to Conflict.", "source_references": "Main p10,p20 / extraction 491–506,1099–1103", "novelty": "Control transfer, repeated benefit and defense"}, "R": {"id": "Q28", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [491, 508]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1124, 1128]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q28", "answer": "A controller gains its listed bonus whenever any player, including the controller, visits Arrakeen, Spice Refinery or Imperial Basin: 1 Solari at Arrakeen or Spice Refinery, 1 spice at Imperial Basin. Winning the corresponding Conflict places your Control marker, replacing an opponent's marker. When the Conflict is revealed for a space you control, you may deploy one troop from your supply directly to Conflict.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Critical Locations: controller receives bonus whenever any player visits; winning sets/replaces control marker; defensive bonus is one troop from supply."}, "B": {"id": "Q28", "answer": "At controlled locations, the controller gains the separate visit bonus whenever any player visits, including if visitor and controller are the same person: 1 Solari at Arrakeen or Spice Refinery, 1 spice at Imperial Basin. Winning that location's Conflict transfers control by placing your marker and replacing an opponent's. When its Conflict is revealed, the controller may deploy one troop from supply directly to the Conflict, without visiting the space.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Critical Locations line 161; board guide line 210 and table lines 225,237,244; defensive bonus is from supply."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q29", "question": "When two players tie for second in a three-player Conflict, what happens? What if players tie for third in four-player play, or three players tie for first?"}, "K": {"id": "Q29", "expected_answer": "Tied second each get third reward; winner keeps first and card, no other rewards. Tied third receive nothing. Three tied first each get second, no winner/card and no further rewards.", "source_references": "Main p14 / extraction 792–808", "novelty": "Remaining combat tie outcome branches"}, "R": {"id": "Q29", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [793, 806]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q29", "answer": "In a three-player tie for second, each tied player gets the third reward; the first-place winner keeps the first reward and card, and no further rewards are given. Players tied for third receive nothing. If three players tie for first, each gets the second reward, nobody takes the Conflict card, and no other rewards are given, including to a remaining fourth player.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Combat ties: tie for second earns third reward for each; tie for third gets nothing. Three tied first gives second reward to each and no other rewards in either player count."}, "B": {"id": "Q29", "answer": "In a three-player tie for second, each tied player gets the third reward; the first-place winner keeps the first reward and Conflict card, with no further rewards. In a four-player tie for third, those tied receive nothing. If three players tie for first, each gets the second reward; no one takes the Conflict card and no other rewards are given, even in a four-player game.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Combat ties, lines 169-181: tie-for-second and tie-for-third outcomes; three tied first rule."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q30", "question": "At a normal three-player Conflict with three different positive strengths, which places receive rewards? What if a two-player game’s Rival is one of the participants?"}, "K": {"id": "Q30", "expected_answer": "Only first and second rewarded, third only used for a tie for second. Two humans plus standard Rival use the same two-/three-player reward rules; Rival competes normally.", "source_references": "Main p14; Supplements p5 Combat; FAQ p1 Conflict", "novelty": "Untied low-player-count rewards"}, "R": {"id": "Q30", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [750, 765]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [317, 325]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [72, 75]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q30", "answer": "In a normal three-player Conflict with three different positive strengths, first and second place receive their rewards and third receives nothing. This is also true when the Rival is a participant in a two-human-plus-Rival game: ordinary first and second rewards are paid, third gets nothing except in a tie for second.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Resolve Combat: with two or three players ordinary first and second receive rewards, third nothing; explicitly includes two humans plus Rival."}, "B": {"id": "Q30", "answer": "With three players at different positive strengths, first and second place receive their rewards; third receives nothing. A Rival counts as a player in the two-human-plus-Rival game, and ordinary third place receives nothing there as well, except that the third reward may be used for a tie for second.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Combat, lines 105-106: ordinary reward ranks by player count; third reward in 2–3 players only for tie for second; Rival is third competitor, line 249."}}

