{"Q": {"id": "Q31", "question": "When can Plot, Combat and Endgame Intrigues be played, how are unplayed Intrigues kept and ordinary ones discarded, and what if the Intrigue deck is exhausted?"}, "K": {"id": "Q31", "expected_answer": "Plot during own Agent/Reveal turns, Combat during Combat with a unit, Endgame at game end. Unplayed face down separate from deck, owner may inspect; played resolved cards face up Intrigue discard. Exhaustion reshuffles Intrigue discard into new deck.", "source_references": "Main p7 / extraction 345–354; FAQ p2 Intrigue cards", "novelty": "Intrigue storage, timing and exhaustion"}, "R": {"id": "Q31", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [338, 352]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [175, 187]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q31", "answer": "Plot Intrigue may be played at any point on your own Agent or Reveal turns; Combat Intrigue only during Combat and only if you have a unit in Conflict; Endgame Intrigue only at game end. Keep unplayed Intrigues face down, separate from your deck, and reveal only when played; after resolving, place face up in discard next to Intrigue Deck. If that deck runs out, shuffle its discard to form a new deck.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Intrigue cards: timing by type, storage and discard; FAQ says if Intrigue deck runs out, shuffle discard to form new deck."}, "B": {"id": "Q31", "answer": "Plot Intrigues may be played during your own Agent or Reveal turn; Combat Intrigues only during Combat and only if you have at least one unit in the Conflict; Endgame Intrigues at the end of the game. Keep unplayed Intrigues face down separate from your deck; after an Intrigue resolves, place it face up in a discard pile by the Intrigue Deck. If that deck runs out, shuffle its discard pile to make a new deck.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Special Rules, lines 166, 286: timing, storage/discard, reshuffle exhausted deck."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q32", "question": "Can you discard an Intrigue for an ordinary discard instruction? Where does an ordinary discard come from? How does Secrets choose which Intrigue is stolen?"}, "K": {"id": "Q32", "expected_answer": "Ordinary discard from hand and cannot be Intrigue unless specified. Secrets steals one random Intrigue from each opponent with four or more, in addition to drawing one from deck and gaining Bene Gesserit Influence.", "source_references": "Main p20 / extraction 1104–1106,1179–1181; Supplements p2; FAQ p2 discard", "novelty": "Discard type and theft threshold"}, "R": {"id": "Q32", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1129, 1131]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1189, 1190]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [114, 119]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [114, 117]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q32", "answer": "An ordinary discard cannot be an Intrigue unless the instruction specifies Intrigue. Ordinary discard is a card of your choice from your hand. Secrets steals one Intrigue selected at random from each opponent who has four or more Intrigue cards.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Discarding: from hand, not in play/discard; cannot be Intrigue unless specified. Secrets: opponents with four or more give one selected at random."}, "B": {"id": "Q32", "answer": "An ordinary discard instruction discards a card of your choice from your hand and cannot discard an Intrigue unless specified. The separate trash-an-Intrigue icon lets you trash one Intrigue of your choice from your hand. Secrets takes one Intrigue selected at random from each opponent who has four or more Intrigues.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Discarding line 168; Trashing line 146; Intrigue/Steal icon line 166."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q33", "question": "Which cards may a trash effect remove, where do ordinary and Reserve cards go, and is trashing optional? Does trashing The Spice Must Flow remove its acquired VP?"}, "K": {"id": "Q33", "expected_answer": "May trash own hand, discard or in-play card. Ordinary to box; Reserve back to its Reserve stack. Optional unless cost or direct self-trash. The Spice Must Flow acquire VP retained after trashing.", "source_references": "Main p20 / extraction 1185–1190; FAQ p4 The Spice Must Flow", "novelty": "Trash locations and persistent acquire VP"}, "R": {"id": "Q33", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1193, 1196]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [334, 335]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q33", "answer": "Trash effects may remove cards from hand, discard pile, or in play. Return ordinary trashed cards to the box; Reserve cards return to their Reserve stack. Trashing is optional unless paying a cost or the card directs you to trash itself. Trashing The Spice Must Flow does not remove VP already gained from its acquire effect.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Trashing section lists eligible zones and destinations; FAQ says Spice Must Flow acquire VP is retained if card is later trashed."}, "B": {"id": "Q33", "answer": "A trash effect may remove a card from your hand, discard pile, or in play. Return ordinary trashed cards to the box; Reserve cards return to their Reserve stack. Trashing is optional unless it pays a cost or a card instructs you to trash itself. Trashing The Spice Must Flow does not remove the VP from its acquire effect; that VP is retained.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Trashing line 146; Victory FAQ line 288: acquire VP retained after trashing."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q34", "question": "When do acquire-box effects resolve, when do you reshuffle your deck, and can unused Persuasion be carried to another round?"}, "K": {"id": "Q34", "expected_answer": "Acquire effect once at acquisition not when later played. Reshuffle discard only when unable to draw due to empty deck then continue. Unspent Reveal Persuasion lost, never saved.", "source_references": "Main pp6,13,20 / extraction 311–317,704–730,1081–1084", "novelty": "Acquire triggers, reshuffle trigger and resource expiration"}, "R": {"id": "Q34", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [300, 302]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [704, 733]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1105, 1107]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q34", "answer": "Acquire-box effects resolve once at the moment you acquire the card. When a draw is needed and your deck is empty, reshuffle your discard pile into a new deck and continue drawing. Unused Persuasion cannot carry over; it is lost at the end of your Reveal turn.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Acquire box resolves at acquisition; acquiring cards says reshuffle discard when unable to draw; unused Persuasion is lost."}, "B": {"id": "Q34", "answer": "An acquire-box effect resolves once at the moment the card is acquired. When you cannot draw because your deck is empty, shuffle the discard pile into a new deck and continue drawing. Unused Persuasion is lost at the end of your Reveal turn and cannot carry over.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Acquire box line 183; Acquiring Cards line 143; reshuffle when deck empty."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q35", "question": "What counts as in play for Fremen Bond, can two Bond cards activate one another regardless of play order, and when do they cease being in play?"}, "K": {"id": "Q35", "expected_answer": "Agent-turn and Reveal cards remain in play face up until Reveal Clean Up unless trashed earlier. Bond requires at least one other Fremen in play; two Bond cards can activate each other regardless of order.", "source_references": "Main p20 / extraction 1111–1117", "novelty": "In-play lifetime and Fremen Bond interaction"}, "R": {"id": "Q35", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1136, 1141]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q35", "answer": "Cards played on Agent turns and cards revealed on your Reveal turn are in play and remain face up through Clean Up, unless trashed first. Two Fremen Bond cards can activate one another regardless of play order. They cease being in play when moved to the discard pile during Clean Up.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "In play / Fremen Bond: both kinds of cards remain in play until Clean Up; two Bond cards activate one another regardless of order."}, "B": {"id": "Q35", "answer": "Cards played on Agent turns and cards revealed during Reveal remain face up and in play until Clean Up, unless trashed earlier. Fremen Bond works if you have one or more other Fremen cards in play; two Bond cards can activate each other regardless of order played. They cease being in play at Clean Up.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "In play / Fremen Bond, line 184."}}

