{"Q": {"id": "Q36", "question": "Can Recall Agent return the Agent placed this turn, and when can the recalled Agent act again? Where does a retreated troop go, and may “retreat any number” mean zero?"}, "K": {"id": "Q36", "expected_answer": "Recall another Agent from board to Leader, not current-turn Agent; can use on later Agent turn same round. Retreat Conflict to garrison; any number permits zero.", "source_references": "Main p20 / extraction 1147–1157; FAQ p3 Retreat", "novelty": "Recall and retreat destinations and reuse"}, "R": {"id": "Q36", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1166, 1168]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1174, 1175]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [255, 256]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q36", "answer": "Recall Agent returns one of your other Agents on the board, not the Agent just placed this turn. The recalled Agent can be used on another Agent turn in the same round. A retreated troop goes from Conflict to your garrison. 'Retreat any number' permits zero.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Recall Agent icon returns another Agent and may be used again same round; Retreat sends troop to garrison; FAQ says retreat any number allows zero."}, "B": {"id": "Q36", "answer": "Recall Agent returns one of your other Agents on the board, not the one just sent this turn; the recalled Agent may be used on another Agent turn in the same round. A retreated troop goes from the Conflict to your garrison. “Retreat any number” includes retreating zero troops.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Recall Agent line 185; Retreat line 186; FAQ line 287."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q37", "question": "When an effect grants two Influence with a freely chosen Faction, may it be split? What is required for an Alliance-icon effect or a minimum-Influence effect?"}, "K": {"id": "Q37", "expected_answer": "Choose one Faction, both Influence there (not split). Alliance effect requires holding shown Faction Alliance token; minimum-Influence effect requires at least shown value with shown Faction.", "source_references": "Main p20 / extraction 1086–1088,1118–1126", "novelty": "Effect eligibility and indivisible Influence"}, "R": {"id": "Q37", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1111, 1113]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1142, 1149]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q37", "answer": "No. When a freely chosen Influence effect grants two, choose one Faction and gain both Influence there. An Alliance-icon effect requires holding that Faction's Alliance token; a minimum-Influence effect requires meeting its stated Influence threshold.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Influence: freely chosen gain two cannot choose two different Factions; Alliance icon requires holding token; some effects require minimum Influence."}, "B": {"id": "Q37", "answer": "A freely chosen gain-two-Influence effect must put both Influence in one Faction; it cannot be split across two. An Alliance icon requires you to hold that Faction's Alliance token. A minimum-Influence effect requires the stated amount with its specified Faction.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Influence rules line 163: free choice gain two cannot choose different Factions; Alliance and minimum Influence requirements."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q38", "question": "If an Alliance holder loses Influence after being tied with two opponents, who receives the token? If the holder drops to 3 and no one has 4, what happens?"}, "K": {"id": "Q38", "expected_answer": "Former holder chooses one of previously tied opponents to receive token; holder loses Alliance VP and receiver gains it. Below 4 loses token; if no eligible 4+ player return token to board, losing its VP.", "source_references": "FAQ p1 Alliance", "novelty": "Alliance loss from retreating holder"}, "R": {"id": "Q38", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [21, 30]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [334, 337]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q38", "answer": "If the Alliance holder loses Influence after being tied, the formerly tied opponent takes the Alliance; if several opponents were tied, the former holder chooses which gets it. If the holder falls to 3 or lower and nobody has 4 or more, return the Alliance token to the board and the holder loses its VP.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Official FAQ—Alliance loss: formerly tied player takes token; among several tied former holder chooses; if holder falls to 3 or lower and nobody has 4+, return it to board."}, "B": {"id": "Q38", "answer": "If the holder loses Influence after being tied with two opponents, the former holder chooses which of those tied opponents receives the Alliance. If the holder falls to 3 or lower and nobody has 4 or more, return the Alliance token to the board and the old holder loses its VP.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Scoring line 153 and FAQ line 282: former holder chooses among multiple tied opponents; return token if none has 4+."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q39", "question": "What happens to a card drawn during Reveal compared with one drawn after Reveal? What happens to a Plot Intrigue played earlier whose effect applies at Reveal?"}, "K": {"id": "Q39", "expected_answer": "During Reveal immediately reveal and use this turn; after Reveal keep until next round, then draw five extra. Plot effect for later Reveal stays face up until that Reveal, use then discard.", "source_references": "FAQ pp2–3 Intrigue cards/Reveal turn", "novelty": "Draw timing branches and delayed Plot duration"}, "R": {"id": "Q39", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [181, 185]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [257, 268]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q39", "answer": "A card drawn during Reveal is immediately revealed and used this turn. A card drawn after Reveal is kept for next round, in addition to the five cards drawn then. A Plot Intrigue played earlier whose effect applies at Reveal stays face up until that Reveal effect is used, then is discarded.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "FAQ—Draw timing: drawn during Reveal means immediately reveal and use this turn; drawn after Reveal means keep for next round; Plot Intrigue with later Reveal effect stays face up until then, is used, then discarded."}, "B": {"id": "Q39", "answer": "A card drawn during Reveal is immediately revealed and used this turn. A card drawn after Reveal is kept for the next round, when the player draws five additional cards. A Plot Intrigue played earlier whose effect applies at Reveal stays face up until then, is used, and then discarded.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "FAQ Draw timing, line 286."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q40", "question": "May a “when you win a Conflict” Intrigue be played after tying for first? What if you receive such an Intrigue as a reward for an outright win?"}, "K": {"id": "Q40", "expected_answer": "Tie for first is not a win, cannot play. An appropriate Intrigue received as winning reward can be played immediately.", "source_references": "FAQ p4 When you win a Conflict", "novelty": "Win-trigger exception and newly gained card timing"}, "R": {"id": "Q40", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [367, 372]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q40", "answer": "No. “When you win” cannot be played after tying for first, because no one wins or takes the card. If received as a reward for an outright win, it may be played immediately.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "FAQ—Combat and troops: “When you win a Conflict” Intrigues cannot be played after tying; if received as winning reward they can be played immediately."}, "B": {"id": "Q40", "answer": "No. A “when you win a Conflict” Intrigue cannot be played after tying for first because no one wins. If you receive that Intrigue as a reward for an outright win, you may play it immediately.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "FAQ Combat and troops, line 287."}}

