{"Q": {"id": "Q41", "question": "What if final VP, spice, Solari, water and garrison troops all remain tied, and may scores exceed 12?"}, "K": {"id": "Q41", "expected_answer": "Final tiebreaker is player who most recently took Reveal turn. Scores may exceed printed track maximum 12.", "source_references": "FAQ p2 Endgame; p4 Victory Points", "novelty": "Final tiebreaker and score boundary"}, "R": {"id": "Q41", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [135, 138]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [364, 366]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q41", "answer": "If VP and all four listed resource tiebreakers remain tied, the player who most recently took a Reveal turn wins. Scores may exceed 12.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "FAQ—Victory: if all four resource tiebreakers remain tied, most recent Reveal turn wins; scores may exceed printed track’s 12."}, "B": {"id": "Q41", "answer": "If final VP and all four listed resource tiebreakers are tied, the player who most recently took a Reveal turn wins. Scores may exceed 12 on the printed track.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Victory FAQ, line 288."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q42", "question": "Can you delay completion of two held contracts for the same board space after visiting, and when in the Agent turn can their effects resolve?"}, "K": {"id": "Q42", "expected_answer": "Completion mandatory; all same-space contracts completed with one Agent placement. Their effects may resolve in any order with space and Agent-box effects; still must hold them at placement.", "source_references": "FAQ p1 contract; Main p16", "novelty": "Mandatory simultaneous contracts and effect ordering"}, "R": {"id": "Q42", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [888, 890]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [76, 85]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q42", "answer": "No. Complete all contracts held for the same space with that one Agent placement; you must have held each contract when sending the Agent. Contract effects are another effect of that Agent turn and may resolve in any order with space and Agent-box effects.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "FAQ—Contract completion: fulfill all same-space contracts with one Agent placement; board-space contract is another effect and can resolve in any order."}, "B": {"id": "Q42", "answer": "No. You must fulfill all contracts you hold for the same space with that one Agent placement. The contract effects are another effect of that Agent turn and can be resolved in any order with the space and Agent-box effects; you must have held the contracts when you sent the Agent.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "FAQ Contract completion, line 283; completion rule line 204."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q43", "question": "Under CHOAM does Shaddam begin with his set-aside Sardaukar contracts, when can he take one, and how long does his Signet Ring deployment restriction last?"}, "K": {"id": "Q43", "expected_answer": "No, not in possession at start. Sardaukar Commander allows acquiring set-aside Sardaukar contract instead of generally available one when taking a contract. Emperor of Known Universe restriction starts immediately with Signet Ring Agent placement and lasts that turn only.", "source_references": "Main p17; FAQ p3 Shaddam Corrino IV", "novelty": "Shaddam contract choice and restriction duration"}, "R": {"id": "Q43", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [948, 951]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [292, 300]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q43", "answer": "Shaddam does not start with the Sardaukar contracts. Before the initial shuffle, set aside both; when acquiring a contract he may choose a set-aside Sardaukar one instead of a generally available one. His Signet Ring deployment restriction takes effect immediately when he plays Signet Ring to send an Agent and lasts for that turn, not the round.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "CHOAM setup and FAQ—Shaddam: set aside both; not initially possessed; may choose one when acquiring; deployment restriction takes effect immediately and lasts that turn."}, "B": {"id": "Q43", "answer": "Shaddam does not begin with the set-aside Sardaukar contracts. Before the contract shuffle, set aside both; when acquiring a contract he may choose a set-aside Sardaukar contract instead of a generally available one. His Emperor of the Known Universe deployment restriction takes effect immediately when he plays Signet Ring to send an Agent, and lasts for that turn only, not the whole round.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "CHOAM setup line 194; Shaddam FAQ line 284 and Leader clarification line 188."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q44", "question": "For Feyd, where does the Training token start and what happens at its last space? Which Jessica side begins face up and can Reverend Mother Jessica act on the flip turn?"}, "K": {"id": "Q44", "expected_answer": "Feyd starts leftmost Training space, stays forever on rightmost once reached. Lady Jessica side starts up, not Reverend Mother. Reverend Mother ability usable on flip turn.", "source_references": "Main p17 / extraction 957–964; FAQ p3 Reverend Mother Jessica", "novelty": "Leader setup and transition timing"}, "R": {"id": "Q44", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [935, 941]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [269, 271]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q44", "answer": "Feyd’s token starts at the leftmost Training track space and stays at the rightmost when it reaches it. Lady Jessica begins face up, not Reverend Mother Jessica; Reverend Mother Jessica may use her ability on the turn she flips.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Leader clarifications: Feyd token starts leftmost and remains rightmost; Lady Jessica begins; FAQ says Reverend Mother Jessica may act on flip turn."}, "B": {"id": "Q44", "answer": "Feyd's token starts on the leftmost space of his Leader's Training track and stays on the rightmost space once it reaches it. Lady Jessica starts with her Lady Jessica side face up, not Reverend Mother Jessica. Reverend Mother Jessica may use her ability on the turn she flips.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Leader clarifications, lines 188-189."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q45", "question": "For Margot and Irulan does moving from 1 to 3 Influence count as reaching 2, can it trigger again later, and does descending through 2 count? Does Clean Up trigger Spacing Guild’s Favor discard ability?"}, "K": {"id": "Q45", "expected_answer": "Passing 2 upward counts, can repeat by losing then regaining Influence; descending does not count. Spacing Guild Favor triggers discard from hand, not in-play-to-discard Clean Up.", "source_references": "Main p17 / extraction 965–978", "novelty": "Threshold crossing and discard-source exception"}, "R": {"id": "Q45", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [942, 954]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q45", "answer": "Moving from 1 to 3 counts as reaching 2. They can reach 2 with the same Faction again after losing Influence and later regaining it; moving down through 2 does not count. Clean Up moving Spacing Guild’s Favor from play to discard does not trigger its discard ability; only discarding it from hand does.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Leader clarifications: reaching 2 while moving past counts and may recur after loss/regain; descending does not. Spacing Guild’s Favor: Clean Up is not discarding from hand."}, "B": {"id": "Q45", "answer": "For Margot and Irulan, moving from 1 to 3 counts as reaching 2 even when passing it while gaining multiple Influence. They can reach 2 again later with the same Faction after losing Influence and regaining it, but moving down through 2 does not count. Clean Up moving Spacing Guild's Favor from in play to discard does not trigger its discard ability; only discarding it from hand does.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Leader clarifications, line 188."}}

