{"Q": {"id": "Q46", "question": "State Accept Contract and Dutiful Service’s Agent icons and effects with and without CHOAM, and whether both automatically advance a Faction track."}, "K": {"id": "Q46", "expected_answer": "Accept Contract: Spice Trade, draw card plus contract or 2 Solari, no automatic Faction Influence. Dutiful Service: Emperor, one Emperor Influence plus contract or 2 Solari. Contract fallback if module off or all contracts taken.", "source_references": "Supplements p1", "novelty": "Nonfaction versus Faction contract spaces"}, "R": {"id": "Q46", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [3, 8]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [37, 43]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q46", "answer": "Accept Contract: Spice Trade icon, no cost, no Combat; always draw one card and resolve contract icon (2 Solari without CHOAM, take/replace a contract with CHOAM if available, otherwise 2 Solari). It is not a Faction space, so no automatic Influence. Dutiful Service: Emperor icon, no cost, no Combat; gain 1 Emperor Influence and resolve same contract icon. Its listed Emperor Influence is the automatic Faction advance counted once, not twice.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board Space Guide: Accept Contract and Dutiful Service rows; contract icon shared rule; Accept is non-Faction, Dutiful Service Emperor and Influence counted once."}, "B": {"id": "Q46", "answer": "Accept Contract uses Spice Trade access, has no cost, always draws one card, and resolves the contract icon: without CHOAM or when all contracts are taken, gain 2 Solari; with available CHOAM contracts, take one. It is not a Faction space and grants no automatic Faction Influence. Dutiful Service uses Emperor access, has no cost, gains 1 Emperor Influence and resolves the same contract icon; it is an Emperor space, so that one automatic Emperor advance is counted once total.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board guide lines 212-230, especially shared contract rule and space table."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q47", "question": "What do Arrakeen, Fremkit and Research Station each cost and provide, what Agent icons access them, and which are Combat spaces?"}, "K": {"id": "Q47", "expected_answer": "Arrakeen City free, troop and card, controller 1 Solari. Fremkit Fremen free, 1 Fremen Influence and card. Research Station City 2 water, two troops and two cards. All Combat.", "source_references": "Supplements pp1–2", "novelty": "Free versus paid card/recruit Combat spaces"}, "R": {"id": "Q47", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [9, 13]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [49, 53]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [104, 108]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q47", "answer": "Arrakeen (City, Combat): no cost; visitor recruits one troop and draws one card, controller gains 1 Solari. Fremkit (Fremen, Combat): no cost; gain 1 Fremen Influence and draw one card. Research Station (City, Combat): pay 2 water; recruit two troops and draw two cards.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board Space Guide rows for Arrakeen, Fremkit and Research Station."}, "B": {"id": "Q47", "answer": "Arrakeen: City access, no cost, Combat space; visitor recruits one troop and draws a card, while controller receives 1 Solari. Fremkit: Fremen access, no cost, Combat space; gain 1 Fremen Influence and draw a card. Research Station: City access, costs 2 water, Combat space; recruit two troops and draw two cards.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board space table, lines 225, 232, 239."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q48", "question": "Compare Deep Desert and Hagga Basin’s entry costs, base spice and worm choices. Do you still collect bonus spice when choosing worms, and are Hooks spent?"}, "K": {"id": "Q48", "expected_answer": "Deep Desert 3 water, 4 spice OR two worms; Hagga 1 water, 2 spice OR one worm. Both collect all bonus spice even with worms. Worm choice requires Maker Hooks, not spent; cannot summon into Shield-Wall-protected Conflict.", "source_references": "Supplements pp1–2; Main p10; FAQ p2 Maker hooks", "novelty": "Maker choice excludes base spice but retains bonus"}, "R": {"id": "Q48", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [19, 26]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [67, 74]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [509, 568]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [200, 201]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q48", "answer": "Deep Desert (Spice Trade, Combat) costs 3 water and offers 4 base spice or, with Maker Hooks, two sandworms; Hagga Basin (Spice Trade, Combat) costs 1 water and offers 2 base spice or, with Hooks, one sandworm. Both give all accumulated bonus spice whichever choice is made. Hooks are not spent when summoning.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board Space Guide rows: Deep Desert and Hagga Basin; Maker rules: visit gains all bonus spice; Hooks retained, not spent."}, "B": {"id": "Q48", "answer": "Deep Desert uses Spice Trade access and costs 3 water; choose 4 base spice or, with Hooks, summon two sandworms. Hagga Basin also uses Spice Trade access and costs 1 water; choose 2 base spice or, with Hooks, summon one sandworm. At either space collect all accumulated bonus spice in addition to the choice. Hooks are retained and not spent.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board space table, lines 227, 234; Hooks not spent, line 133."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q49", "question": "For each Sietch Tabr option, state requirements and effects. Do you get a troop when choosing to remove the Shield Wall?"}, "K": {"id": "Q49", "expected_answer": "City access, 2+ Fremen Influence, no resource cost. Option one Hooks if needed, one troop, one water; option two one water and may remove wall. Option two gives no troop or Hooks. Combat space.", "source_references": "Supplements p2", "novelty": "Sietch mutually exclusive option branches"}, "R": {"id": "Q49", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [127, 136]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q49", "answer": "Both Sietch Tabr options require City access and 2+ Fremen Influence, with no resource entry cost. Option one: take Maker Hooks if lacking them, recruit one troop, gain 1 water. Option two: gain 1 water and optionally remove the Shield Wall; it gives no troop.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board Space Guide: Sietch Tabr row, including requirements and two choices."}, "B": {"id": "Q49", "answer": "Both Sietch Tabr choices require City access, 2+ Fremen Influence, and no resource entry cost. Choice one: take Maker Hooks if you lack them, recruit one troop, and gain 1 water. Choice two: gain 1 water and optionally remove the Shield Wall. The second choice does not grant a troop.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board space table, line 243."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q50", "question": "How do High Council’s first and subsequent visits differ, what does each cost, when is its ongoing benefit used, and is it a Combat space?"}, "K": {"id": "Q50", "expected_answer": "Landsraad 5 Solari each visit. First Councilor to empty seat, +2 Persuasion each Reveal rest of game; later 2 spice, Intrigue, three troops. Not Combat, cannot normally deploy recruited troops.", "source_references": "Supplements p2", "novelty": "High Council persistent upgrade versus revisit rewards"}, "R": {"id": "Q50", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [81, 89]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q50", "answer": "High Council is Landsraad, non-Combat. Each visit costs 5 Solari. First visit puts your Councilor on an unoccupied seat and grants 2 Persuasion on every Reveal turn for the rest of the game. Later visits grant 2 spice, draw an Intrigue, and recruit three troops.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board Space Guide: High Council row."}, "B": {"id": "Q50", "answer": "High Council uses Landsraad access, costs 5 Solari each visit, and is not a Combat space. On the first visit put your Councilor on an unoccupied seat and gain 2 Persuasion on each Reveal turn for the rest of the game. Subsequent visits give 2 spice, draw an Intrigue, and recruit three troops.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board space table, line 236."}}

