{"Q": {"id": "Q51", "question": "What does Swordmaster cost before and after anyone obtains one, how often may each player visit, and when can the new Agent be used? Does a Rival obtaining it lower human cost?"}, "K": {"id": "Q51", "expected_answer": "Landsraad 8 Solari before any Swordmaster, then 6; once per player per game. Third Agent from beside board onto Leader immediately usable same round and rest of game. Rival also lowers cost.", "source_references": "Supplements p2; FAQ p3 Rivals", "novelty": "Swordmaster dynamic cost and immediate action capacity"}, "R": {"id": "Q51", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [143, 152]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [287, 289]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q51", "answer": "Swordmaster costs 8 Solari before anyone obtains one and 6 thereafter; each player may gain it only once. Take the third Agent from beside the board to your Leader; it is available this round and for the rest of the game. A Rival gaining Swordmaster also reduces human cost to 6.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board Space Guide: Swordmaster row."}, "B": {"id": "Q51", "answer": "Swordmaster uses Landsraad access and is not a Combat space. It costs 8 Solari before anyone gains Swordmaster and 6 after anyone does. Each player may take it only once per game. The third Agent becomes available this round and for the rest of the game. A Rival obtaining its Swordmaster also lowers the human cost to 6.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board space table, line 245."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q52", "question": "State Imperial Privilege’s Agent icon, requirement, entry cost and effects. Which Agent can it recall and does it automatically give Emperor Influence?"}, "K": {"id": "Q52", "expected_answer": "Landsraad, 2+ Emperor Influence, 3 Solari. May discard Intrigue to draw Intrigue; recall another Agent and draw card. Not the current Agent. No automatic Emperor Influence.", "source_references": "Supplements p2; Main p20", "novelty": "Recall-space requirement versus Faction gain"}, "R": {"id": "Q52", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [96, 103]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1166, 1168]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q52", "answer": "Imperial Privilege is Landsraad, requires 2+ Emperor Influence and costs 3 Solari; it is non-Combat. You may discard an Intrigue to draw one, and recall one of your other Agents and draw a card. It gives no automatic Emperor Influence.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board Space Guide: Imperial Privilege row; Faction status notes: this is not a Faction space."}, "B": {"id": "Q52", "answer": "Imperial Privilege uses Landsraad access; it requires 2+ Emperor Influence and costs 3 Solari. Its effects let you discard an Intrigue to draw an Intrigue, recall one of your other Agents, and draw a card. It does not automatically give Emperor Influence; it is a Landsraad space, not an Emperor Faction space.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board space table, line 238; Faction status distinctions, line 210."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q53", "question": "State Shipping’s access icon, Influence requirement, cost and gains. Does its free-choice Influence have to be with the Guild?"}, "K": {"id": "Q53", "expected_answer": "Spice Trade, 2+ Guild Influence, 3 spice. Gain 5 Solari and one Influence any one Faction, not necessarily Guild.", "source_references": "Supplements p2", "novelty": "Shipping qualifying Faction versus chosen gain"}, "R": {"id": "Q53", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [120, 126]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q53", "answer": "Shipping is Spice Trade access, requires 2+ Spacing Guild Influence, costs 3 spice, and is non-Combat; gain 5 Solari and 1 Influence with any one Faction. The free-choice Influence need not be Guild.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board Space Guide: Shipping row; Spice Trade is not a Faction."}, "B": {"id": "Q53", "answer": "Shipping uses Spice Trade access, requires 2+ Spacing Guild Influence, and costs 3 spice. It gains 5 Solari and 1 Influence with any one Faction; the Influence need not be Guild.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board space table, line 242."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q54", "question": "Compare Gather Support and Spice Refinery’s zero-cost and paid options and Combat status."}, "K": {"id": "Q54", "expected_answer": "Gather Support Landsraad choose 0/2 Solari, two troops either way, plus one water if paid, not Combat. Refinery City choose 0/1 spice, gain 2/4 Solari respectively, controller 1 Solari either way, Combat.", "source_references": "Supplements pp1–2", "novelty": "Optional entry costs and different deployment access"}, "R": {"id": "Q54", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [54, 58]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [137, 142]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q54", "answer": "Gather Support is Landsraad, non-Combat: choose to pay 0 or 2 Solari; recruit two troops either way, and if you pay 2 also gain 1 water. Spice Refinery is City, Combat: choose 0 or 1 spice; gain 2 Solari for free or 4 if you paid 1; controller gains 1 Solari.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board Space Guide rows: Gather Support and Spice Refinery."}, "B": {"id": "Q54", "answer": "Gather Support uses Landsraad access, is not Combat, and lets you choose to pay 0 or 2 Solari: recruit two troops either way, and paying 2 also gains 1 water. Spice Refinery uses City access, is Combat, and lets you pay 0 or 1 spice: gain 2 Solari free or 4 Solari if paying 1; its controller separately gains 1 Solari.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board space table, lines 233, 244."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q55", "question": "State Heighliner, Desert Tactics and Sardaukar’s entry costs, Influence gains, recruits and other effects; which allow normal deployment?"}, "K": {"id": "Q55", "expected_answer": "Heighliner 5 spice, Guild Influence +1 and five troops, Combat. Desert Tactics 1 water, Fremen Influence +1 and one troop, optional trash, Combat. Sardaukar 4 spice, Emperor Influence +1 and four troops plus Intrigue, not Combat.", "source_references": "Supplements pp1–2", "novelty": "Faction recruit spaces with different Combat flags"}, "R": {"id": "Q55", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [31, 36]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [75, 80]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [109, 113]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q55", "answer": "Heighliner: Spacing Guild, Combat, costs 5 spice; gain 1 Guild Influence and recruit five troops. Desert Tactics: Fremen, Combat, costs 1 water; gain 1 Fremen Influence, recruit one troop, optionally trash a card. Sardaukar: Emperor, non-Combat, costs 4 spice; gain 1 Emperor Influence, draw an Intrigue and recruit four troops. Only Heighliner and Desert Tactics permit normal deployment.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board Space Guide rows: Heighliner, Desert Tactics, Sardaukar."}, "B": {"id": "Q55", "answer": "Heighliner: Spacing Guild access, 5 spice, gain 1 Guild Influence and recruit five troops; Combat permitted. Desert Tactics: Fremen access, 1 water, gain 1 Fremen Influence, recruit one troop, optionally trash a card; Combat permitted. Sardaukar: Emperor access, 4 spice, gain 1 Emperor Influence, draw an Intrigue and recruit four troops; Combat not permitted.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board space table, lines 229, 235, 240."}}

