{"Q": {"id": "Q56", "question": "What are Assembly Hall, Espionage and Deliver Supplies’s Agent icons, costs and effects, including Assembly Hall’s timing condition?"}, "K": {"id": "Q56", "expected_answer": "Assembly Hall Landsraad free, Intrigue now, 1 Persuasion at Reveal if own Agent there. Espionage BG 1 spice, 1 BG Influence, card and Spy. Deliver Supplies Guild free, 1 Guild Influence and 1 water. None Combat.", "source_references": "Supplements p1", "novelty": "Persistent location conditional and resource/spy spaces"}, "R": {"id": "Q56", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [14, 18]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [27, 30]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [44, 48]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q56", "answer": "Assembly Hall (Landsraad, no cost, non-Combat) draws an Intrigue and gives 1 Persuasion during your Reveal turn if your Agent is there. Espionage (Bene Gesserit, 1 spice, non-Combat) gains 1 Bene Gesserit Influence, draws a card and places a Spy. Deliver Supplies (Spacing Guild, no cost, non-Combat) gains 1 Guild Influence and 1 water.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board Space Guide rows: Assembly Hall, Espionage, Deliver Supplies."}, "B": {"id": "Q56", "answer": "Assembly Hall uses Landsraad access, costs nothing, is not Combat; draw an Intrigue, and if your Agent is there gain 1 Persuasion during your Reveal turn. Espionage uses Bene Gesserit access, costs 1 spice, is not Combat; gain 1 Bene Gesserit Influence, draw a card, place a Spy. Deliver Supplies uses Spacing Guild access, costs nothing, is not Combat; gain 1 Guild Influence and 1 water.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board space table, lines 226, 228, 231."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q57", "question": "What must False Orders’ affected opponents do, may it be played without an opposing Spy connected to your destination, and when is Litany Against Fear’s red box ignored?"}, "K": {"id": "Q57", "expected_answer": "Each affected opponent moves Spy to empty observation post not connected to this turn Agent destination. Can play without enemy Spy there. Litany red box ignored during Reveal or with gained Agent icon when played normally as Agent card.", "source_references": "FAQ pp2–3 False Orders/Litany Against Fear", "novelty": "Specific movement and card-box exceptions"}, "R": {"id": "Q57", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [140, 145]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [192, 195]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q57", "answer": "False Orders moves affected opponents’ Spies to empty posts not connected to your Agent’s destination that turn; it may be played even if no enemy Spy is connected there. Ignore Litany Against Fear’s red box during Reveal, or when it gains an Agent icon and is played normally as an Agent card.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "FAQ—False Orders and Litany Against Fear."}, "B": {"id": "Q57", "answer": "False Orders makes affected opponents move their Spy to an empty post not connected to your Agent's destination that turn. It may be played even if no enemy Spy is connected there. With Litany Against Fear, ignore its red box during Reveal, or when it gains an Agent icon and is played normally as an Agent card.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "FAQ, line 289."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q58", "question": "With Manipulate, may opponents acquire the removed card, may you acquire it by other means with the discount, and when does an unacquired card leave the game?"}, "K": {"id": "Q58", "expected_answer": "Opponents cannot acquire. You may use other means but 1-Persuasion discount does not apply. If not acquired by end of next Reveal turn, remove from game.", "source_references": "FAQ p3 Manipulate", "novelty": "Removed-row card access and expiry"}, "R": {"id": "Q58", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [205, 212]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q58", "answer": "Opponents cannot acquire the card removed by Manipulate. You may acquire it by other means, but without the 1-Persuasion discount; if unacquired by the end of your next Reveal, remove it from the game.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "FAQ—Manipulate."}, "B": {"id": "Q58", "answer": "Opponents cannot acquire the card removed by Manipulate. You may acquire it by other means, but without the 1-Persuasion discount. If not acquired by the end of your next Reveal, remove it from the game.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "FAQ Manipulate, line 289."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q60", "question": "What components and resource does the standard two-player Rival start with, what happens to the 2P Reshuffle card, and can its 10 VP trigger Endgame and victory?"}, "K": {"id": "Q60", "expected_answer": "Four cubes at Influence bottoms, three garrison troops rest supply, two Agents supply and third beside board, three Spies and one water supply, score/Combat zero. Retain Reshuffle in Hagal. Scoring Rival can trigger end at 10+ and win.", "source_references": "Supplements p3; Main p5", "novelty": "Rival full setup and scoring threat"}, "R": {"id": "Q60", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [157, 165]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [194, 204]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [271, 275]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q60", "answer": "Rival setup: give it a color, four cubes at bottom of Influence tracks, three troops in garrison and remaining troops in supply, two Agents in supply and Swordmaster beside board, three Spies and 1 water in supply; score and Combat marker start at 0. Shuffle House Hagal and retain the 2P Reshuffle card. Rival’s 10+ VP triggers Endgame and it can win.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Required Rival Rules—Setup and opening: listed components; retains Reshuffle; Rival can win and 10+ VP triggers Endgame."}, "B": {"id": "Q60", "answer": "The Rival starts with a color, four Influence cubes at the bottom of tracks, three troops in its garrison and the rest in supply, two Agents in supply and Swordmaster beside the board, three Spies and 1 water in supply; its score and Combat marker start at 0. Shuffle House Hagal and retain the 2P Reshuffle card. The Rival can reach 10+ VP and trigger Endgame at Recall like a human; it can win by having the most VP.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival setup and win condition, lines 249, 251."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q61", "question": "When does a Rival buy Swordmaster, how does it count and prioritize spending resources, does it keep leftovers, and is its Agent available immediately?"}, "K": {"id": "Q61", "expected_answer": "As soon as total resources reaches printed value; Solari spice Intrigues water each unit one. Spend only threshold, prioritizing Solari then spice then Intrigue then water; keep leftovers. Third Agent immediately available including current round.", "source_references": "Supplements p5; p2 Swordmaster; FAQ p3 Rivals", "novelty": "Automated mixed-resource upgrade timing"}, "R": {"id": "Q61", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [289, 293]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [143, 152]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q61", "answer": "As soon as its total of Solari, spice, Intrigue cards and water reaches its printed Swordmaster threshold, spend that many and take its third Agent, usable that round. Spend Solari first, then spice, Intrigue cards, water; keep leftovers.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival—Resources and Swordmaster."}, "B": {"id": "Q61", "answer": "When the Rival's combined Solari, spice, Intrigue cards, and water reach its printed Swordmaster value, each unit counts as one resource; it spends that many resources and takes its third Agent, available in the current round. It spends Solari first, then spice, then Intrigue cards, then water, keeping leftovers. The new Agent is immediately usable this round.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Resources and Swordmaster, line 261."}}

