{"Q": {"id": "Q62", "question": "After a Rival has Swordmaster, which exact resource sets does it spend for VP, and can it spend a mixed total of seven resources for a VP?"}, "K": {"id": "Q62", "expected_answer": "Each set 7 Solari, 7 spice, 3 Intrigues or 3 water gives 1 VP whenever available. No mixed seven-resource VP purchase; mixed total only used for Swordmaster.", "source_references": "Supplements p5 Buying Victory Points diagram", "novelty": "Rival homogeneous conversion thresholds"}, "R": {"id": "Q62", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [309, 316]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements-p5.png", "sha256": "5e24b5ed4a6540818579c78da86364909ea7798b6c3e9f0485ccf3eeb4ebc024", "region": "Buying Victory Points, upper-right; all four icon rows"}]}, "A": {"id": "Q62", "answer": "After Swordmaster, it spends each set of 7 Solari, 7 spice, 3 Intrigue cards, or 3 water for 1 VP. The thresholds are separate exact sets; a mixed total of seven is not specified as a scoring set.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival—Resources and Swordmaster: “7 Solari,” “7 spice,” “3 Intrigue cards,” or “3 water.”"}, "B": {"id": "Q62", "answer": "After obtaining Swordmaster, the Rival spends each set of 7 Solari, 7 spice, 3 Intrigue cards, or 3 water for 1 VP. It does not convert a mixed total of seven resources into a VP; the listed sets are exact individual resource thresholds.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Resources and Swordmaster, line 261."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q63", "question": "When choosing Influence, how does a Rival select the Faction and break ties? Does it get VP at 2 and Alliance VP, or the track bonus at 4? What does a numbered Hagal Influence icon mean?"}, "K": {"id": "Q63", "expected_answer": "Choose least Influence, ties leftmost priority. Gains/losses of Influence VP and Alliance VP as humans, no 4-track bonus. Number means Faction at that position in printed priority list.", "source_references": "Supplements pp4–5; Main p7", "novelty": "Rival priority and track-bonus exception"}, "R": {"id": "Q63", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [239, 243]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [272, 272]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [326, 327]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [329, 337]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q63", "answer": "Choose the Faction with least Influence, breaking ties by leftmost priority icon. Rival gets Influence VP and Alliance VP like a human, but not the resource track bonus at 4. A numbered Hagal Influence icon refers to that position in its priority list.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival—Resources/Swordmaster and Agent turns."}, "B": {"id": "Q63", "answer": "When choosing Influence, the Rival chooses the Faction with least Influence, breaking ties by leftmost priority icon. It gains Influence VP at 2 and Alliance VP when holding an Alliance like a human; it does not get the resource/track bonus for reaching 4 Influence. A numbered Hagal Influence icon means that position in its Faction priority list.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival rules, lines 257, 261, 275."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q64", "question": "A Rival reveals a two-destination Hagal card and the condition-selected destination is occupied. Can it use the other destination, and what conditions select these cards?"}, "K": {"id": "Q64", "expected_answer": "Cannot switch to other; reveal again. Accept Contract/Shipping based on Guild Influence; Deliver Supplies/Heighliner based on Conflict tier I/II/III. Use card printed condition.", "source_references": "Supplements p4 Special Instructions; FAQ p3 Rivals", "novelty": "Rival conditional destination cannot fallback"}, "R": {"id": "Q64", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [273, 281]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [276, 281]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q64", "answer": "No. Choose only the destination matching the current condition (Guild Influence for Accept Contract/Shipping; Conflict tier for Deliver Supplies/Heighliner). If it is occupied, reveal a new card without using the other destination.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival—Agent turns: two-destination selection and occupied destination rule."}, "B": {"id": "Q64", "answer": "No. The Rival selects only the condition-matching destination; if it is occupied, it reveals a new Hagal card instead of using the other destination. The conditions are Guild Influence for Accept Contract/Shipping, and Conflict tier for Deliver Supplies/Heighliner.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Agent turns, line 253."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q65", "question": "A Rival has no troops newly recruited by a card sending it to Combat. Can it deploy garrison troops? What if a Hagal card recruits at a noncombat space or has a conditional 2-Influence bonus not met?"}, "K": {"id": "Q65", "expected_answer": "Still deploy up to two available garrison troops at Combat. New troops at noncombat go garrison. Missing 2-Influence bonus does not block placement, just no bonus. Use only Hagal effects, not ordinary board effects.", "source_references": "Supplements p4", "novelty": "Rival deployment and conditional bonus failure"}, "R": {"id": "Q65", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [237, 250]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [270, 281]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q65", "answer": "Yes. At every Combat space it deploys up to two troops available in garrison even if the card recruited none. Troops recruited at a non-Combat space go to garrison. Conditional 2+ Influence bonuses do not prevent placement; if unmet, only that bonus is absent.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival—Agent turns: at Combat deploy up to two garrison troops; recruit icons; conditional bonus never prevents placement."}, "B": {"id": "Q65", "answer": "Yes, at every Combat space the Rival may deploy up to two available garrison troops even if the card recruited none. Troops recruited at a noncombat space go into garrison. A conditional 2+ Influence bonus not met does not prevent placing the Agent; it only means the bonus is not applied.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival rules, lines 257-258: recruits deploy at Combat or enter garrison otherwise; always up to two garrison troops; conditional bonus does not block placement."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q66", "question": "How does a Rival choose an unrestricted Spy post, what happens if all Faction posts are occupied, and what occurs on placing its third Spy? Can it Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence?"}, "K": {"id": "Q66", "expected_answer": "First available Faction post by priority; if all full ignore placement. Third/final supply Spy placed triggers immediately recalling other two and printed Scheme. Never Infiltrate/Gather Intelligence.", "source_references": "Supplements pp4–5", "novelty": "Rival automated spy placement and Scheme trigger"}, "R": {"id": "Q66", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [254, 264]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [334, 342]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q66", "answer": "Unless a post type is specified, place Spy at the first available Faction observation post in priority order; if all four occupied, ignore placement. Placing its third and final supply Spy recalls its other two and triggers its Scheme. Rivals never Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival—Spies and Schemes."}, "B": {"id": "Q66", "answer": "Unless a type is specified, the Rival places a Spy at the first available Faction observation post in its priority order; if all four are occupied, it ignores placement. Placing its third and final supply Spy immediately recalls its other two and triggers its Scheme. Rivals never recall Spies to Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Spies and Schemes, line 259."}}

