{"Q": {"id": "Q67", "question": "If a Rival’s Scheme recruits troops before a Hagal Agent reaches a Combat space on that same turn, what happens to those troops? What if a Place Spy card found no legal post?"}, "K": {"id": "Q67", "expected_answer": "Deploy Scheme recruits on same-turn Combat placement. Place Spy card still followed by another Hagal reveal whether placement succeeds or not, because no Agent has been sent.", "source_references": "Supplements pp4–5", "novelty": "Scheme recruitment timing before placement"}, "R": {"id": "Q67", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [259, 264]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [343, 347]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q67", "answer": "Scheme-recruited troops before Agent placement deploy too if the Rival visits a Combat space that turn. If Place Spy finds no legal post, ignore placement and immediately reveal another Hagal card because no Agent was sent.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival—Spies and Schemes; Place Spy cards do not place an Agent."}, "B": {"id": "Q67", "answer": "If the Scheme recruits troops before the Rival's Agent placement and it then visits a Combat space on the same turn, deploy those troops too. A Place Spy card does not send an Agent; if no legal post exists, ignore placement and immediately reveal another Hagal card to continue the Agent turn.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival rules, lines 255, 259."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q68", "question": "At Hagga Basin or Deep Desert, how does a Rival choose worms versus base spice with Hooks, without Hooks, or with a protected Conflict? What happens to accumulated bonus spice?"}, "K": {"id": "Q68", "expected_answer": "Always take bonus spice. With Hooks and summonable Conflict summons one at Hagga/two Deep instead of base. Without Hooks or if protected, summons none and gains base spice (2/4). At Imperial Basin gains base1. Hagal wall removal requires Hooks.", "source_references": "Supplements p5; p4 icons", "novelty": "Rival mandatory worm choice and fallback"}, "R": {"id": "Q68", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [294, 308]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [265, 269]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [19, 26]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [67, 74]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q68", "answer": "It always takes all accumulated bonus spice. At Hagga Basin or Deep Desert, if it has Hooks and the Conflict permits worms, it summons one or two worms respectively instead of base spice; without Hooks or when protected, it takes base spice (2 or 4).", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival—Maker spaces."}, "B": {"id": "Q68", "answer": "At Hagga Basin or Deep Desert with Hooks and a Conflict that permits worms, the Rival summons one or two worms respectively instead of base spice. Without Hooks, or if the Conflict is protected by Shield Wall, it summons none and takes base spice (Hagga 2, Deep Desert 4). It always collects all bonus spice there. Hooks are not spent.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Maker spaces line 263; Hooks retained line 133."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q69", "question": "When and how is a Rival’s Combat strength bonus determined, what if Reshuffle appears, and can humans respond afterward? Does a unit-free Rival get this bonus?"}, "K": {"id": "Q69", "expected_answer": "Start Combat in turn order, only with deployed unit: one Hagal card, bottom swords only added. Reshuffle and draw again on Reshuffle. Humans then Combat Intrigue before resolution. No unit no bonus.", "source_references": "Supplements p5 Combat", "novelty": "Automated bonus precedes human response"}, "R": {"id": "Q69", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [317, 320]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q69", "answer": "At Combat start, if Rival has at least one deployed unit, reveal a Hagal card in turn order and add its bottom swords to strength. On Reshuffle, reshuffle and reveal again. Humans then take their normal Combat Intrigue window. Unit-free Rival gets no bonus.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival—Combat."}, "B": {"id": "Q69", "answer": "At Combat start, if the Rival has at least one unit deployed, reveal one Hagal card in turn order and add its bottom swords as strength; if Reshuffle appears, reshuffle and reveal again. Humans then have their normal Combat Intrigue window. A Rival with no unit deployed does not get this bonus.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Combat, line 275."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q70", "question": "Can a Rival gain control, defensive troops, battle-icon VP and doubled rewards? How does it handle optional Conflict VP payments and contract rewards with CHOAM?"}, "K": {"id": "Q70", "expected_answer": "Normal control visit bonus and defensive supply troop; win card/match icons; sandworms double. Always buy optional Conflict VP if can pay resources or required Spy recall. Never contracts; each contract reward becomes 2 Solari even with CHOAM.", "source_references": "Supplements p5 Combat", "novelty": "Rival reward choices and module exception"}, "R": {"id": "Q70", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [321, 332]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q70", "answer": "Yes: it gains control bonuses, defensive troop from supply, battle-icon VP, and doubles rewards with one or more worms. It always takes an optional Conflict VP if able to pay resources or recall required Spies. It never takes contracts; a contract reward gives 2 Solari even with CHOAM.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival—Combat: control/reward rules, optional VP and contract rule."}, "B": {"id": "Q70", "answer": "Yes: it gains control bonuses and the defensive troop when its controlled Conflict is revealed, wins Conflict cards and battle-icon VP normally, and doubles rewards with one or more worms. It always takes an optional Conflict VP if it can pay the resources or recall required Spies. It never takes contracts; even with CHOAM a contract reward gives it 2 Solari.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Combat, line 275."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q71", "question": "When during Reveal do you total, announce and set Combat strength, can you update it during the turn, and how is strength over 20 marked?"}, "K": {"id": "Q71", "expected_answer": "After Reveal Cards and before Clean Up, at any point while resolving effects; announce total, set marker and update as needed. Above20 flip +20 side and count again from beginning of track.", "source_references": "Main pp12–13 / extraction 652–665,733–738", "novelty": "Flexible strength-setting timing and marker overflow"}, "R": {"id": "Q71", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [657, 674]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [734, 738]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q71", "answer": "During Reveal effects, total and announce strength and set the Combat marker at any point; update it as needed while resolving the turn. Over 20, flip marker to +20 side and start again from the track beginning.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Strength and Reveal Turn: marker may be set at any point while resolving and updated; over 20 use +20 side."}, "B": {"id": "Q71", "answer": "During Reveal resolution, total and announce Combat strength and set the marker at any point; you may update it as needed while resolving. Strength over 20 is marked by flipping to the +20 side and starting again from the beginning of the track.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Reveal Turn, line 99; Strength, line 123."}}

