{"Q": {"id": "Q72", "question": "When is a Leader’s Signet Ring ability activated, does merely revealing Signet Ring activate it, and can card text override normal game rules?"}, "K": {"id": "Q72", "expected_answer": "Activated when playing Signet Ring on an Agent turn, not when merely revealing. Left Leader ability used as described. Cards of any type can override normal rules.", "source_references": "Main p6,p20 / extraction 306–310,327–329,1162–1164", "novelty": "Generic Signet trigger and rules precedence"}, "R": {"id": "Q72", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [291, 295]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [312, 313]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1180, 1181]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q72", "answer": "A Leader’s Signet Ring ability activates when you play Signet Ring on an Agent turn, not merely when you reveal it. Card text may override the usual rules.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup—Leaders: Signet Ring ability activates on Agent turn; Overview: cards of any type can override usual rules."}, "B": {"id": "Q72", "answer": "A Leader's Signet Ring ability activates when you play Signet Ring on one of your Agent turns, not merely when you reveal it. Card text can override the usual rules of the game.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup, line 54; Overview, line 25."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q73", "question": "How is a Recall Spy icon on a card resolved, where does the Spy go, and is it automatically the same as Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence?"}, "K": {"id": "Q73", "expected_answer": "Return one of own Spies from observation post to supply, usually a cost for card effect. Card recall distinct from the two voluntary recalls for Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence; it does not automatically give either benefit.", "source_references": "Main p11,p20 / extraction 603–605,1150–1151", "novelty": "Card recall destination versus voluntary recall purpose"}, "R": {"id": "Q73", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [590, 606]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1169, 1170]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q73", "answer": "Recall Spy icon returns one of your Spies from a post to your supply, typically as a cost. It is not automatically Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence; those are separate choices when recalling without a card.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Special Rules—Spies & observation posts."}, "B": {"id": "Q73", "answer": "A Recall Spy icon returns one of your Spies from an observation post to your supply, usually as a cost for an effect. The icon itself does not automatically Infiltrate or Gather Intelligence; those are separate effects available by recalling a Spy without a card for their stated purposes.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Special Rules, line 160."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q74", "question": "What does the “trash an Intrigue” icon allow you to choose, as opposed to an ordinary discard-a-card instruction?"}, "K": {"id": "Q74", "expected_answer": "Trash an Intrigue of choice from own hand. Ordinary discard chooses a non-Intrigue from hand unless explicitly specified.", "source_references": "Main p20 / extraction 1104–1106,1184", "novelty": "Dedicated Intrigue trash versus ordinary deck discard"}, "R": {"id": "Q74", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1129, 1131]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1192, 1192]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q74", "answer": "The trash-an-Intrigue icon trashes one Intrigue of your choice from your hand. Ordinary discard cannot select Intrigue unless specified and is from your hand.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Trashing and Discarding sections."}, "B": {"id": "Q74", "answer": "The trash-an-Intrigue icon trashes one Intrigue of your choice from your hand. An ordinary discard instruction instead discards a card of your choice from your hand and cannot be an Intrigue unless specified; discard does not mean trash.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Trashing, line 146; Discarding, line 168."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q75", "question": "A Conflict reward grants one Influence of your choice and is doubled by your sandworm. May the two gains go to different Factions? Contrast a single effect that grants two Influence."}, "K": {"id": "Q75", "expected_answer": "Yes. Sandworm doubling of a one-Influence reward gives two separate gains, which may use the same Faction or two different Factions. A single two-Influence effect instead chooses just one Faction and cannot be split.", "source_references": "Main PDF p14 Sandworm Reward Doubling example and p20 Influence icons / extraction 778–791,1123–1126", "novelty": "Explicit doubled-reward Influence split exception versus indivisible two-Influence effect"}, "R": {"id": "Q75", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [779, 787]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1147, 1149]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q75", "answer": "Yes. A doubled reward offering 1 Influence gives two gains and may use the same or two different Factions. By contrast, one freely chosen gain-two Influence effect requires both with one Faction.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Sandworm Reward Doubling: doubled 2 Influence may use same or two different; Influence rule: gain two freely chosen cannot split."}, "B": {"id": "Q75", "answer": "Yes, a doubled reward that grants 1 Influence of your choice may be taken twice, with the same Faction or two different Factions. A single effect granting two Influence with free choice requires both gains with the same one Faction; it cannot split them.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Sandworm Reward Doubling, line 137; Influence, line 163."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q76", "question": "A House Hagal card shows a Signet Ring effect for the two-player Rival. Which ability is resolved, and does the Rival need a human Signet Ring card or a Reveal turn to trigger it?"}, "K": {"id": "Q76", "expected_answer": "Resolve the Signet Ring ability printed on the selected Rival card as the Hagal effect. No human deck Signet Ring card or Reveal turn is involved; Rival never Reveals.", "source_references": "Supplements PDF pp3–4 Rival card anatomy and House Hagal Signet Ring icon", "novelty": "Rival Hagal Signet trigger distinct from human Signet Ring Agent-card trigger"}, "R": {"id": "Q76", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [167, 181]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [226, 246]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q76", "answer": "Resolve the Rival card’s printed Signet Ring ability; it does not need a human Signet Ring card or Reveal turn.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival setup: follow its printed Signet Ring and Scheme abilities; it never Reveals."}, "B": {"id": "Q76", "answer": "Resolve the Rival card's printed Signet Ring ability when Hagal shows a Signet Ring effect. It does not need a human Signet Ring card and never takes a Reveal turn; the Rival follows its printed Signet Ring and Scheme abilities as directed by its Rival card/Hagal effects.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival overview/Agent turns, lines 249, 257; Rival never Reveals, line 253."}}

