{"Q": {"id": "Q77", "question": "For a two-player Rival, what do House Hagal Maker Hooks and Shield Wall removal icons do if it already has Hooks, lacks Hooks, or the wall is already gone?"}, "K": {"id": "Q77", "expected_answer": "Maker Hooks icon takes a token onto garrison only if Rival lacks one. Shield Wall removal effect removes the wall if Rival has Hooks and wall remains; without Hooks ignore the removal effect, and if wall already gone no wall remains to remove.", "source_references": "Supplements PDF p4 Hagal icon explanations", "novelty": "Rival-only prerequisite on wall removal, and idempotent Hooks acquisition"}, "R": {"id": "Q77", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [265, 269]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q77", "answer": "Maker Hooks icon gives a token only if it lacks one. Shield Wall removal works only if it has Hooks and Wall remains; without Hooks or if already removed, ignore/no further effect.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Hooks and Wall icons table."}, "B": {"id": "Q77", "answer": "Maker Hooks icon: take a token from the bank if the Rival lacks one; if it already has Hooks, do not take another. Shield Wall removal: remove the Wall only if it has Hooks and the Wall remains; if it lacks Hooks, ignore it, and if the Wall is already gone it has no further effect.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Rival Hooks and Wall icons, lines 265-273."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q78", "question": "For Secrets, state its Agent icon, entry cost, Combat status and all effects, including which Intrigues come from the deck and which come from opponents."}, "K": {"id": "Q78", "expected_answer": "Bene Gesserit, no cost, not Combat. Gain one BG Influence and draw one Intrigue from deck. Each opponent with four or more Intrigues gives one randomly selected Intrigue; below four gives none.", "source_references": "Supplements PDF p2 Secrets; Main p7 Intrigue and p20 Steal Intrigue", "novelty": "Complete Secrets space procedure; prior Q32 asks only theft selection, not separate deck draw/Influence/access/Combat status"}, "R": {"id": "Q78", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [114, 119]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1189, 1190]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q78", "answer": "Secrets is Bene Gesserit, costs nothing, non-Combat; gain 1 Bene Gesserit Influence and draw an Intrigue from the deck. Each opponent with 4+ Intrigues gives one selected at random.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board Space Guide—Secrets row."}, "B": {"id": "Q78", "answer": "Secrets uses Bene Gesserit access, costs nothing, is not a Combat space, gains 1 Bene Gesserit Influence and draws one Intrigue from the Intrigue Deck. Each opponent with four or more Intrigues must give one selected at random; these come from opponents, not the deck.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board space table, line 241; Intrigue rules line 166."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q79", "question": "For Imperial Basin, state its Agent icon, entry cost and Combat status, how much base and bonus spice the visiting player receives, and what its controller receives if that same player controls it."}, "K": {"id": "Q79", "expected_answer": "Spice Trade, no entry cost, Combat. Visitor gains one base spice plus all accumulated bonus spice. Controller gains one additional spice whenever anyone visits, including self; a controlling visitor receives both gains.", "source_references": "Supplements PDF p2 Imperial Basin; Main p10 control", "novelty": "Imperial Basin base-spice procedure, plus self-controller benefit; prior Maker and control questions never request this complete visit outcome"}, "R": {"id": "Q79", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-supplements.txt", "sha256": "ce8e2d26252d71fb45e531b07160b494059c13ebb37f0668b9cd86a4c5854315", "lines": [90, 95]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [501, 505]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q79", "answer": "Imperial Basin is Spice Trade, no cost, Combat. Visitor gains 1 base spice plus all bonus spice; controller gains 1 spice. If visitor also controls it, both effects apply, so it gains that additional 1 spice.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board Space Guide—Imperial Basin row; controlled locations resolve both visitor and controller effects."}, "B": {"id": "Q79", "answer": "Imperial Basin uses Spice Trade access, has no cost, and is a Combat space. The visitor receives 1 base spice plus all accumulated bonus spice; its controller receives 1 spice. If the visitor is also controller, that player receives both the visitor's spice and the separate 1-spice control bonus.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Board guide lines 210, 237."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q80", "question": "At Round Start, where is the newly revealed Conflict placed, what happens to any unclaimed Conflict card left from earlier rounds, and does each player draw the round’s five cards before or after revealing the Conflict?"}, "K": {"id": "Q80", "expected_answer": "Reveal top Conflict face up in space next to deck, on top of any Conflict cards still there from earlier rounds. Then each player draws five; card not won in previous round is not taken into a player supply by this placement.", "source_references": "Main PDF p8 / extraction 355–360", "novelty": "Current/unclaimed Conflict card destination and replacement order, previously only key background in Q23"}, "R": {"id": "Q80", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [354, 358]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q80", "answer": "Reveal new Conflict from top and place it face up next to deck, on top of any Conflict cards remaining from prior rounds; then each player draws five cards.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Phase 1: Round Start."}, "B": {"id": "Q80", "answer": "At Round Start, reveal a new Conflict from the top and place it face up next to the deck, on top of any Conflict cards left from earlier rounds. Resolve the controlled-location defensive troop bonus, then each player draws five cards; therefore the Conflict is revealed before the hand draw.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Round Start, line 88."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q81", "question": "At standard human setup, where do the four Faction Influence cubes and Alliance tokens begin, does anyone start with an Alliance, and is the Shield Wall initially present?"}, "K": {"id": "Q81", "expected_answer": "Each human puts one cube at bottom of each of four Influence tracks, starting at zero Influence. Alliance tokens are on their marked track spaces, not held by players; nobody starts allied. Shield Wall starts present in marked area below Spice Refinery, protecting its three locations until removed.", "source_references": "Main PDF pp4–5 and p10 / extraction 239–246,274–278,506–522", "novelty": "Initial unclaimed Alliances/zero human Influence and initially active protection, distinct from later threshold/transfer questions"}, "R": {"id": "Q81", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [220, 227]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [274, 277]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [509, 523]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q81", "answer": "Each player puts one cube on the bottom space of each of four Faction Influence tracks; Alliance tokens begin on their marked track areas, so no player starts holding one. Shield Wall token is placed on the board below Spice Refinery.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup steps 1 and 6."}, "B": {"id": "Q81", "answer": "Each human's four cubes start on the bottom spaces of the four Faction Influence tracks. The four Alliance tokens start on the marked areas of those tracks; no human starts holding an Alliance. The Shield Wall token is initially placed in the marked area below Spice Refinery.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup, lines 52, 57."}}

