{"Q": {"id": "Q82", "question": "In a normal three- or four-player round, who takes the first Player Turn, how does turn order proceed after someone Reveals, and exactly when does Player Turns end? During Combat Intrigue, who has first priority, in which direction does priority proceed, and how many Combat Intrigues may an eligible player play before yielding?"}, "K": {"id": "Q82", "expected_answer": "Player Turns starts with the First Player marker and proceeds clockwise one turn at a time. Skip anyone who has already Revealed; the phase ends when all players have Revealed. Combat Intrigue likewise begins with First Player and proceeds clockwise among players with at least one unit in the Conflict; each may play any number or pass.", "source_references": "Main PDF pp8,14; run extraction lines397–459,813–826", "novelty": "Turn priority, skipped players and phase termination are not requested by Q03/Q08/Q23; Q19 only asks the two-player Rival order. Any-number Combat permission is also unasked."}, "R": {"id": "Q82", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [360, 376]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [743, 746]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q82", "answer": "First Player starts, turns proceed clockwise, one at a time; a player who Reveals is skipped for rest of phase; in 3–4 player play phase ends when all have Revealed. During Combat Intrigue, First Player then clockwise; eligible players may play any number or pass, with the window closing after all involved pass consecutively.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Player Turns and Combat phase."}, "B": {"id": "Q82", "answer": "The player with the First Player marker takes the first turn, then play continues clockwise, one turn at a time. A player who Reveals is skipped for the remainder of the phase; in three- or four-player play Player Turns end once all players have Revealed. Combat Intrigue priority begins with First Player and continues clockwise. An eligible player may play any number of Combat Intrigues before passing; the window ends after all involved players pass consecutively.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Player Turns line 91; Combat line 103."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q83", "question": "What are the three steps of a Reveal turn, in order? Must the Reveal-box effects be resolved in card order, or may the player choose their order?"}, "K": {"id": "Q83", "expected_answer": "Reveal Cards, Resolve Reveal Effects, Clean Up, in that order. Reveal all remaining hand cards first; resolve their Reveal effects in any chosen order; then clean up all played cards.", "source_references": "Main PDF p12; run extraction lines714–748", "novelty": "Q03 asks card eligibility/destination, Q13 purchase interleaving and Q71 strength timing; none requests the Reveal step sequence or effect-order freedom."}, "R": {"id": "Q83", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [646, 677]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q83", "answer": "Reveal Cards; Resolve Reveal Effects; Clean Up. Reveal effects may be resolved in any order, not card order.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Reveal Turn: three steps and effects in any order."}, "B": {"id": "Q83", "answer": "The steps are: Reveal Cards (reveal the remaining hand), Resolve Reveal Effects (resolve just those cards' Reveal boxes and acquire with Persuasion as desired), then Clean Up (move all cards in front to discard). Reveal effects may be resolved in any order, not necessarily card order.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Reveal Turn, lines 97-100."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q84", "question": "Before the first round without CHOAM, how are each human starter deck, Intrigue deck, Imperium deck/Row and Reserve stacks prepared? Where do the human Combat marker, three Spies, Councilor and Control markers start?"}, "K": {"id": "Q84", "expected_answer": "Each human shuffles their identical ten-card starting deck and puts it face down in their supply left of their Leader. Omit CHOAM-marked Imperium/Intrigue cards, shuffle the Intrigue and Imperium decks face down, deal five Imperium cards face up, and place Prepare the Way and The Spice Must Flow in separate Reserve stacks next to the Row. Human Combat marker starts at zero on the indicated initial side; three Spies, Councilor and Control markers start in their supply in clear view.", "source_references": "Main PDF pp3–5; run extraction lines102–319, especially C1–C3/E/G3/G6", "novelty": "Initial deck/market preparation and the remaining human component destinations are not requested by Q01/Q02/Q16/Q21/Q60/Q81. These establish playable initial state; not a numerical variant of an existing setup question."}, "R": {"id": "Q84", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [105, 126]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [200, 211]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [231, 235]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [266, 283]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q84", "answer": "Shuffle each human’s 10-card starting deck and place face down by Leader. Omit CHOAM cards absent module; shuffle Intrigue and Imperium decks separately, face down; deal five face-up Imperium Row cards; place Prepare the Way and The Spice Must Flow as separate Reserve stacks. Combat marker starts at 0; three Spies, Councilor, and Control markers remain in supply; cubes start on bottom Faction spaces.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup steps 4 and 6; Initial card states."}, "B": {"id": "Q84", "answer": "Shuffle each human's 10-card starting deck and put it face down in their supply; without CHOAM omit CHOAM-marked cards from Imperium and Intrigue decks, shuffle each separately face down, and deal five Imperium cards face up as the Row; put Prepare the Way and The Spice Must Flow in separate Reserve stacks. Each human Combat marker starts at 0; three Spies, Councilor, and Control markers remain in the player's supply; the four Influence cubes instead start at the bottom of the tracks.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup lines 55-58; initial card states line 76; human components line 57."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q85", "question": "Which cards may you ordinarily acquire with Persuasion, where is each acquisition cost shown, and during which kind of your turn may you make those ordinary Persuasion purchases?"}, "K": {"id": "Q85", "expected_answer": "During the player’s Reveal turn, acquire any available card from the five-card Imperium Row or Prepare the Way/The Spice Must Flow from the Reserve, paying the Persuasion cost printed at the top right. Ordinary Persuasion purchasing is a Reveal-turn procedure.", "source_references": "Main PDF p13 Acquiring Cards and p20 Persuasion; run extraction lines775–806,1256–1259", "novelty": "Q13 asks spending within Reveal, pooling, replacement and destination; it does not ask the legal purchase sources, printed price or whether an Agent turn permits ordinary purchases. Q34 only asks acquire-box/reshuffle rules."}, "R": {"id": "Q85", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [704, 733]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1163, 1165]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q85", "answer": "Ordinarily acquire any of the five face-up Imperium Row cards, Prepare the Way, or The Spice Must Flow; cost at top right. Spend Persuasion during your Reveal turn.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Acquiring Cards."}, "B": {"id": "Q85", "answer": "During your Reveal turn, Persuasion can ordinarily buy any of the five Imperium Row cards or either Reserve card, Prepare the Way or The Spice Must Flow. Each card's cost is at its top right. Ordinary purchases happen during Reveal, not Agent turns.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Acquiring Cards, line 143; Card anatomy line 93."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q86", "question": "When a human receives a Spy placement icon or a Recall Spy icon, may the player decline the action even if a legal Spy/post exists? Does a Shield Wall destruction icon require destruction, and if destroyed can the Wall return in a later round?"}, "K": {"id": "Q86", "expected_answer": "Ordinary Spy placement and ordinary Recall Spy are permissive: may place/recall. An unpaid optional recall cost gives no associated benefit; Intrigue costs/conditions still must be met to play that Intrigue. Shield Wall destruction is optional. Once removed, return it to the box; it is gone for the rest of the game.", "source_references": "Main PDF pp10–11; FAQ pp3–4 optional effects/Shield Wall; run main lines577–585,646–665; FAQ lines217–228,304–306", "novelty": "Q26 asks placement legality, Q73 asks recall resolution/destination and Q49 asks Sietch option outcomes, but none expressly requests these human icon optionality branches or Wall permanence. Q77 is Rival-specific and uses different mandatory automation."}, "R": {"id": "Q86", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [519, 523]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [580, 592]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [175, 180]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-official-faq-2025-01-13.txt", "sha256": "783b74f6aea9b4f0512e68a0581ca0438cb42dd565e2d88e0778b1322ecb5f23", "lines": [304, 306]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q86", "answer": "Ordinary Spy placement and Recall Spy actions are optional. Shield Wall removal is optional (“may remove”); once removed it is returned to box and cannot return.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Special Rules—Spies; Shield Wall."}, "B": {"id": "Q86", "answer": "Ordinary Spy placement and Recall Spy icons are optional even when legal. A Shield Wall destruction icon may be declined. If destroyed, the Wall is removed for the rest of the game and cannot return in a later round.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Special Rules, lines 160, 162: Spy actions optional; Shield Wall may be removed and cannot return."}}

