{"Q": {"id": "Q99", "question": "After all players have finished their Reveal turns, a Combat Intrigue changes a participant's deployed units or strength while that participant still has a unit in the Conflict. Must their Combat marker change during the Combat Intrigue window, or does the Reveal-turn value stay fixed until cleanup? Which strength is used to determine Conflict rewards?"}, "K": {"id": "Q99", "expected_answer": "Adjust the participant's Combat marker on the Combat track to reflect the changed units or strength when the card resolves. Their Reveal-turn total is not fixed for the rest of the round. Resolve Combat after all involved players pass consecutively, using the adjusted strength shown on the track for rewards. If a later effect removes their last unit, their strength becomes zero.", "source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "pdf_pages": [14], "lines": [817, 824]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "pdf_pages": [14], "lines": [744, 752]}], "novelty": "Main p14 explicitly prescribes an ongoing phase-3 update after strength was set during Reveal. Q08 asks pass/re-entry/closure and post-reward unit destinations; its key alone says adjust strength for effects, which receives no coverage credit. Q71 asks updates during the Reveal turn, not during Combat. Q07 asks the unit/sword formula and last-unit-zero exception, not maintaining a nonzero participant's marker after a Combat Intrigue resolves. Q69 asks only the separate automatic Rival bonus. Q91 asks reset after rewards. The new claim is this consequential Combat-window timing/procedure; the final-unit-zero and consecutive-pass reminders are repeated context only. No named-card or changed-number variant is proposed."}, "R": {"id": "Q99", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [743, 750]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q99", "answer": "Yes. Adjust Combat marker when the Combat Intrigue resolves; Reveal-turn strength is not fixed. Combat resolves using adjusted strength shown on track after all participants pass consecutively.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Combat phase: adjust marker during Intrigue window; resolve with adjusted strength."}, "B": {"id": "Q99", "answer": "The Combat marker must be adjusted when the Combat Intrigue resolves during the Combat Intrigue window if it changes deployed units or otherwise alters strength. The Reveal value is not fixed until cleanup; rewards use the adjusted strength shown on the track after all involved players pass consecutively.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Combat, line 103."}}
{"Q": {"id": "Q100", "question": "When an ordinary effect tells you to gain Solari, spice or water, where do the gained resource tokens come from? May you take them from another player’s supply instead?"}, "K": {"id": "Q100", "expected_answer": "Take ordinary resource gains from the common bank. Do not take them from another player’s supply.", "source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/docs/quality/summary-qa/dune-imperium-uprising/2026-11-04-batch-231507/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "pdf_page": 20, "lines": [1281, 1283]}, {"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "pdf_page": 20, "lines": [1171, 1173]}], "novelty": "Accept exactly one grouped question for the single general resource-gain origin rule. Do not create separate Solari, spice and water variants. This is not a changed amount/name within a tested branch: an ordinary gain from the bank leaves opponents’ holdings intact, whereas taking from another player changes two players’ holdings. The source explicitly defines that legal origin. Q22’s correct incidental key clause cannot substitute for an actual requested question part."}, "R": {"id": "Q100", "corrected_authoritative_source_references": [{"file": "/home/jonny/projects/boardgame-rules/extracted/dune-imperium-uprising-rules.txt", "sha256": "21342cf965b4c64456776adea86f44d4ebf60815cebae4eb6c86187bf02fb580", "lines": [1171, 1173]}]}, "A": {"id": "Q100", "answer": "Take gains from the common bank; payments return to the bank. The summary does not say to take resources from another player; they are bank-supplied.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup step 7: take gains from bank, return payments to bank."}, "B": {"id": "Q100", "answer": "Gained Solari, spice, and water come from the bank; the rules do not take them from another player's supply. Payments of those resources are returned to the bank.", "support": "supported", "evidence": "Setup, line 58."}}
